window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-2"]={"id":"CGL-30-SEP-2026-SHIFT-2","title":"CGL 30 SEP 2026 SHIFT 2","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000069981","section":"REASONING","topic":"Clock & Calendar","question":{"en":"The Mumbai seminar was 4 days after the Ahmedabad seminar. The Pune seminar was 1 day before the Mumbai seminar. If the Ahmedabad seminar was held on 15<sup>th</sup> July, when was the Pune seminar? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"मुंबई सेमिनार अहमदाबाद सेमिनार के 4 दिन बाद था। पुणे सेमिनार मुंबई सेमिनार से 1 दिन पहले था। यदि अहमदाबाद सेमिनार 15 जुलाई को हुआ, तो पुणे सेमिनार कब हुआ? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"17<sup>th</sup> July","hi":"17 जुलाई"},"2":{"en":"18<sup>th</sup> July","hi":"18 जुलाई"},"3":{"en":"19<sup>th</sup> July","hi":"19 जुलाई"},"4":{"en":"20<sup>th</sup> July","hi":"20 जुलाई"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Ahmedabad was on 15 July, so Mumbai, which was 4 days later, was on 15 + 4 = 19 July<br>Pune was 1 day before Mumbai, so Pune was on 19 − 1 = 18 July<br>Hence the Pune seminar was on 18<sup>th</sup> July<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 18<sup>th</sup> July.</b>","hi":"अहमदाबाद 15 जुलाई को था, अतः 4 दिन बाद वाला मुंबई सेमिनार 15 + 4 = 19 जुलाई को था<br>पुणे मुंबई से 1 दिन पहले था, अतः पुणे 19 − 1 = 18 जुलाई को था<br>इसलिए पुणे सेमिनार 18 जुलाई को हुआ<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 18 जुलाई है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000069982","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Analogy","question":{"en":"If 19 &#8594; 91, 82 &#8594; 28, then 75 &#8594; ? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि 19 &#8594; 91, 82 &#8594; 28, तो 75 &#8594; ? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"57"},"2":{"en":"58"},"3":{"en":"65"},"4":{"en":"75"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"In each pair the two digits of the number are written in the reverse order: 19 becomes 91 and 82 becomes 28 ✔<br>So the digits of 75 are simply reversed<br>Hence 75 &#8594; 57<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 57.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक युग्म में संख्या के दोनों अंक उलटे क्रम में लिखे जाते हैं: 19 से 91 तथा 82 से 28 ✔<br>अतः 75 के अंक केवल उलट दिए जाते हैं<br>इसलिए 75 &#8594; 57<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 57 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000069983","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"<b>Statement:</b><br>The Reserve Bank has mandated that banks shall not process any high-value interbank transactions through manual channels beyond business hours, and such transactions shall only be facilitated via authorized electronic platforms.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. High-value interbank transactions are permissible outside business hours if routed through approved digital systems.<br>II. Manual processing of large interbank transactions is prohibited entirely, irrespective of timing. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कथन:<br>भारतीय रिज़र्व बैंक ने अनिवार्य किया है कि बैंक कार्य समय के बाद किसी भी उच्च-मूल्य अंतर-बैंक लेन-देन को मैनुअल माध्यमों से संसाधित नहीं करेंगे, और ऐसे लेन-देन केवल अधिकृत इलेक्ट्रॉनिक प्लेटफ़ॉर्म के माध्यम से ही किए जाएँगे।<br>निष्कर्ष:<br>I. यदि स्वीकृत डिजिटल प्रणालियों से किया जाए तो कार्य समय के बाद भी उच्च-मूल्य अंतर-बैंक लेन-देन की अनुमति है।<br>II. बड़े अंतर-बैंक लेन-देन की मैनुअल प्रोसेसिंग समय की परवाह किए बिना पूरी तरह प्रतिबंधित है। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही II निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Both conclusion I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The mandate stops manual processing only after business hours and allows such transactions through authorised electronic platforms, so such transactions are permissible outside business hours when digital systems are used, and conclusion I follows<br>The ban on manual channels is limited to beyond business hours, so the words prohibited entirely make conclusion II too wide and it does not follow<br>Hence only conclusion I follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Only conclusion I follows.</b>","hi":"आदेश केवल कार्य समय के बाद मैनुअल प्रोसेसिंग रोकता है और अधिकृत इलेक्ट्रॉनिक प्लेटफ़ॉर्म से ऐसे लेन-देन की अनुमति देता है, अतः डिजिटल प्रणालियों के प्रयोग पर कार्य समय के बाद भी ऐसे लेन-देन की अनुमति है और निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br>मैनुअल माध्यमों पर प्रतिबंध केवल कार्य समय के बाद तक है, अतः 'पूरी तरह प्रतिबंधित' कहना निष्कर्ष II को अत्यधिक व्यापक बना देता है और वह नहीं निकलता<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000069984","section":"REASONING","topic":"Age Problems","question":{"en":"The average age of 3 friends is 27. If a new friend joins, the average becomes 28. What is the age of the new friend? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"3 मित्रों की औसत आयु 27 वर्ष है। यदि एक नया मित्र जुड़ता है, तो औसत 28 हो जाता है। नए मित्र की आयु क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"29"},"2":{"en":"30"},"3":{"en":"31"},"4":{"en":"32"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The total age of the 3 friends is 3 × 27 = 81<br>With the new friend the total age of 4 persons is 4 × 28 = 112<br>So the age of the new friend is 112 − 81 = 31<br>Hence the new friend is 31 years old<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 31.</b>","hi":"3 मित्रों की कुल आयु 3 × 27 = 81 है<br>नए मित्र के साथ 4 व्यक्तियों की कुल आयु 4 × 28 = 112 है<br>अतः नए मित्र की आयु 112 − 81 = 31 है<br>इसलिए नया मित्र 31 वर्ष का है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 31 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000069985","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"3 people can do a job in 12 days. How many people are needed to finish it in 4 days? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"3 व्यक्ति एक कार्य को 12 दिनों में कर सकते हैं। उसे 4 दिनों में पूरा करने के लिए कितने व्यक्ति चाहिए? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6"},"2":{"en":"8"},"3":{"en":"9"},"4":{"en":"12"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The work needs 3 × 12 = 36 person-days<br>To finish the same work in 4 days the number of people needed is 36 ÷ 4 = 9<br>Hence 9 people are needed<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 9.</b>","hi":"कार्य के लिए 3 × 12 = 36 व्यक्ति-दिन चाहिए<br>वही कार्य 4 दिनों में पूरा करने के लिए आवश्यक व्यक्ति 36 ÷ 4 = 9 हैं<br>इसलिए 9 व्यक्तियों की आवश्यकता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 9 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000069986","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Complete the pattern: 24, 16, 48, 32, 96 [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"पैटर्न पूरा कीजिए: 24, 16, 48, 32, 96 [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"100"},"2":{"en":"64"},"3":{"en":"78"},"4":{"en":"36"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The series changes alternately by −8 and ×3: 24 − 8 = 16, 16 × 3 = 48, 48 − 16 = 32 and 32 × 3 = 96 ✔<br>So the step after 96 is again a subtraction of 32, giving 96 − 32 = 64<br>Hence the next term is 64<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 64.</b>","hi":"श्रेणी में बारी-बारी −8 तथा ×3 होता है: 24 − 8 = 16, 16 × 3 = 48, 48 − 16 = 32 तथा 32 × 3 = 96 ✔<br>अतः 96 के बाद फिर घटाव 96 − 32 = 64 देता है<br>इसलिए अगला पद 64 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 64 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000069987","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Course of Action","question":{"en":"<b>Statement:</b> More young people are addicted to social media.<br><b>Course of Action:</b><br>1. Promote awareness about digital wellness.<br>2. Ban all social media platforms. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कथन: अधिक से अधिक युवा सोशल मीडिया के आदी हो रहे हैं।<br>कार्यवाही का क्रम:<br>1. डिजिटल स्वास्थ्य के बारे में जागरूकता बढ़ाना।<br>2. सभी सोशल मीडिया प्लेटफ़ॉर्म पर प्रतिबंध लगाना। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only 1","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"Only 2","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both follow","hi":"दोनों"},"4":{"en":"Neither follows","hi":"कोई नहीं"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Addiction to social media is best handled by teaching people to use these platforms sensibly, so spreading awareness about digital wellness is a practical and proportionate step, and course of action 1 follows<br>Banning every platform is neither practical nor desirable for young people who also use them for study and work, so course of action 2 does not follow<br>Hence only 1 follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only 1.</b>","hi":"सोशल मीडिया की लत का सही उपाय लोगों को इन मंचों का समझदारी से उपयोग सिखाना है, अतः डिजिटल स्वास्थ्य पर जागरूकता फैलाना व्यावहारिक और संतुलित कदम है और कार्यवाही 1 निकलती है<br>हर प्लेटफ़ॉर्म पर प्रतिबंध न व्यावहारिक है न उचित, क्योंकि युवा इनका उपयोग पढ़ाई और काम के लिए भी करते हैं, अतः कार्यवाही 2 नहीं निकलती<br>इसलिए केवल 1 निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल 1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000069988","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"How many centres were there if the roll numbers are: 223456, 223478, 224123, 225987, 223999 [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि रोल नंबर 223456, 223478, 224123, 225987, 223999 हैं, तो कितने केंद्र थे? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"3"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The centre is decided by the first three digits of the roll number<br>223456, 223478 and 223999 all begin with 223, so they belong to one centre<br>224123 begins with 224 and 225987 begins with 225, so they belong to two more centres<br>Hence there were 3 centres in all<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 3.</b>","hi":"केंद्र रोल नंबर के पहले तीन अंकों से तय होता है<br>223456, 223478 तथा 223999 सभी 223 से शुरू होते हैं, अतः ये एक ही केंद्र के हैं<br>224123 224 से तथा 225987 225 से शुरू होते हैं, अतः ये दो अन्य केंद्रों के हैं<br>इसलिए कुल 3 केंद्र थे<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000069989","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Identify the number that does not belong to the group: [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"वह संख्या पहचानिए जो समूह में नहीं आती: [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1441"},"2":{"en":"2197"},"3":{"en":"2744"},"4":{"en":"3375"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"2197 = 13³, 2744 = 14³ and 3375 = 15³, so these three are perfect cubes<br>1441 is not a perfect cube (11³ = 1331 and 12³ = 1728), so it does not belong to the group<br>Hence 1441 is the number that does not belong to the group<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 1441.</b>","hi":"2197 = 13³, 2744 = 14³ तथा 3375 = 15³, अतः ये तीनों पूर्ण घन हैं<br>1441 पूर्ण घन नहीं है (11³ = 1331 तथा 12³ = 1728), अतः यह समूह में नहीं आता<br>इसलिए 1441 वह संख्या है जो समूह में नहीं आती<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 1441 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000069990","section":"REASONING","topic":"Seating & Mixed Arrangement","question":{"en":"Direction: Study the following information carefully and answer the questions given below.<br>In a soft toy shop, eight boxes are kept in the form of a stack. The boxes are numbered in ascending order from 1 to 8 such that the topmost box is numbered as 1 while the bottom-most box is numbered as 8. Each box contains different soft toys – Mickey Mouse, Dog, Rabbit, Teddy Bear, Whale, Tiger, Monkey, and Duck.<br>The box of Teddy bear is kept at the top. There are four boxes between the box of Teddy bear and the box of Duck. The box of Monkey is kept between the box of Rabbit and box number 6. Neither the box of Dog nor the box of Rabbit is kept at the bottom. The box of Whale is kept above the box of Tiger, which is kept above the box of Rabbit.<br>Which soft toy does box number 2 contain? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निर्देश: निम्नलिखित जानकारी ध्यान से पढ़िए और नीचे दिए प्रश्नों के उत्तर दीजिए।<br>एक खिलौना दुकान में आठ बक्से ढेर के रूप में रखे हैं। बक्सों की संख्या 1 से 8 तक बढ़ते क्रम में है, जहाँ सबसे ऊपर का बक्सा 1 तथा सबसे नीचे का बक्सा 8 है। प्रत्येक बक्से में भिन्न खिलौना है – Mickey Mouse, Dog, Rabbit, Teddy Bear, Whale, Tiger, Monkey तथा Duck।<br>Teddy bear का बक्सा सबसे ऊपर है। Teddy bear के बक्से तथा Duck के बक्से के बीच चार बक्से हैं। Monkey का बक्सा Rabbit के बक्से तथा बक्सा संख्या 6 के बीच है। न तो Dog का और न ही Rabbit का बक्सा सबसे नीचे है। Whale का बक्सा Tiger के बक्से के ऊपर है, और Tiger का बक्सा Rabbit के बक्से के ऊपर है।<br>बक्सा संख्या 2 में कौन-सा खिलौना है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Whale","hi":"व्हेल"},"2":{"en":"Rabbit","hi":"खरगोश"},"3":{"en":"Tiger","hi":"बाघ"},"4":{"en":"Monkey","hi":"बंदर"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Teddy bear is in box 1, and with four boxes between Teddy bear and Duck, Duck must be in box 6<br>Whale is above Tiger and Tiger is above Rabbit, so these three occupy three consecutive higher places, and Monkey lies between Rabbit and box 6, which fixes Whale in box 2, Tiger in box 3, Monkey in box 4 and Rabbit in box 5<br>Dog is not at the bottom, so Dog is in box 7 and Duck in box 6, while the remaining toy takes box 8<br>Hence box number 2 contains Whale<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Whale.</b>","hi":"Teddy bear बक्सा 1 में है और उसके तथा Duck के बीच चार बक्से होने से Duck बक्सा 6 में होगा<br>Whale, Tiger के ऊपर तथा Tiger, Rabbit के ऊपर है, अतः ये तीन क्रमागत ऊपरी स्थानों पर हैं, और Monkey, Rabbit तथा बक्सा 6 के बीच है, जिससे Whale बक्सा 2, Tiger बक्सा 3, Monkey बक्सा 4 तथा Rabbit बक्सा 5 में तय होते हैं<br>Dog सबसे नीचे नहीं है, अतः Dog बक्सा 7 में तथा Duck बक्सा 6 में है, और शेष खिलौना बक्सा 8 में<br>इसलिए बक्सा संख्या 2 में Whale है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): व्हेल है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000069991","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"Direction: Study the following information carefully to answer the given questions:<br>If 'A @ B' means 'B is a brother of A'<br>If 'A # B' means 'B is the mother of A'<br>If 'A % B' means 'B is the father of A'<br>If 'A &amp; B' means 'B is a sister of A'<br>If 'R # C % V &amp; X' is given, then who among the following is a child of C? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निर्देश: दी गई जानकारी ध्यान से पढ़कर प्रश्न का उत्तर दीजिए:<br>यदि 'A @ B' का अर्थ है 'B, A का भाई है'<br>यदि 'A # B' का अर्थ है 'B, A की माता है'<br>यदि 'A % B' का अर्थ है 'B, A का पिता है'<br>यदि 'A &amp; B' का अर्थ है 'B, A की बहन है'<br>यदि 'R # C % V &amp; X' दिया है, तो निम्न में से C की संतान कौन है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"R"},"2":{"en":"X"},"3":{"en":"V"},"4":{"en":"Both R and X","hi":"R और X दोनों"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"R # C means C is the mother of R, so R is the child of C ✔<br>C % V means V is the father of C, so V is not a child of C ✘<br>V &amp; X means X is the sister of V, so X belongs to the older generation and is not a child of C ✘<br>So only R is a child of C<br>Hence the answer is R<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): R.</b>","hi":"R # C का अर्थ है C, R की माता है, अतः R, C की संतान है ✔<br>C % V का अर्थ है V, C का पिता है, अतः V, C की संतान नहीं ✘<br>V &amp; X का अर्थ है X, V की बहन है, अतः X पिछली पीढ़ी का है और C की संतान नहीं ✘<br>अतः केवल R, C की संतान है<br>इसलिए उत्तर R है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): R है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000069992","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"Rearrange the letters of that word, written in capital letters, to form the correct word.<br>The chef decided to NTERAIMA the succulent steak for several hours to enhance its flavor. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"बड़े अक्षरों में लिखे उस शब्द के अक्षरों को व्यवस्थित करके सही शब्द बनाइए।<br>The chef decided to NTERAIMA the succulent steak for several hours to enhance its flavor. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"MARTINE"},"2":{"en":"REMINAT"},"3":{"en":"MARINATE"},"4":{"en":"RAIMENT"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The jumbled letters NTERAIMA contain M, A, R, I, N, A, T and E<br>Rearranging them with the meaning of soaking food before cooking gives the word MARINATE, which fits the sentence exactly<br>The other options are not meaningful words that fit the blank<br>Hence the correct word is MARINATE<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): MARINATE.</b>","hi":"अव्यवस्थित अक्षर NTERAIMA में M, A, R, I, N, A, T तथा E हैं<br>पकाने से पहले भोजन को भिगोने के अर्थ के साथ इन्हें व्यवस्थित करने पर MARINATE बनता है, जो वाक्य में ठीक बैठता है<br>अन्य विकल्प अर्थपूर्ण शब्द नहीं हैं जो रिक्त स्थान में फिट हों<br>इसलिए सही शब्द MARINATE है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): MARINATE है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000069993","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Analogy","question":{"en":"Find the number that best completes the analogy. D : 32 :: J : ? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"वह संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए जो सादृश्य पूरा करती है। D : 32 :: J : ? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"70"},"2":{"en":"72"},"3":{"en":"80"},"4":{"en":"76"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The position of D in the alphabet is 4, and 4 × 8 = 32 ✔<br>The position of J is 10, so the matching number is 10 × 8 = 80<br>Hence the answer is 80<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 80.</b>","hi":"वर्णमाला में D का स्थान 4 है और 4 × 8 = 32 ✔<br>J का स्थान 10 है, अतः संबंधित संख्या 10 × 8 = 80 है<br>इसलिए उत्तर 80 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 80 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000069994","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Choose the correct option to complete the series.<br>Day : Night :: Victory : ? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"श्रेणी पूरी करने के लिए सही विकल्प चुनिए।<br>Day : Night :: Victory : ? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Success","hi":"सफलता"},"2":{"en":"Celebration","hi":"उत्सव"},"3":{"en":"Triumph","hi":"विजय"},"4":{"en":"Defeat","hi":"पराजय"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Day and night are opposites of each other<br>So the fourth word must be the opposite of victory, which is defeat<br>Success and triumph mean almost the same as victory and celebration is what follows a victory<br>Hence the answer is Defeat<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Defeat.</b>","hi":"Day तथा Night एक-दूसरे के विपरीत हैं<br>अतः चौथा शब्द victory का विपरीत होना चाहिए, अर्थात् defeat<br>Success तथा Triumph लगभग victory के समान अर्थ रखते हैं और Celebration विजय के बाद आता है<br>इसलिए उत्तर Defeat है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): पराजय है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000069995","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Choose the correct option to complete the series.<br>Citrus : Lemon :: Rosaceae : ? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"श्रेणी पूरी करने के लिए सही विकल्प चुनिए।<br>Citrus : Lemon :: Rosaceae : ? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Hibiscus","hi":"हिबिस्कस"},"2":{"en":"Mango","hi":"आम"},"3":{"en":"Pear","hi":"नाशपाती"},"4":{"en":"Cleopatra","hi":"क्लियोपेट्रा"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Lemon belongs to the citrus family of fruits<br>In the same way the answer must be a fruit of the Rosaceae family, and pear belongs to the rose family ✔<br>Hibiscus belongs to the mallow family and mango to the cashew family, while Cleopatra is not a plant at all<br>Hence the answer is Pear<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Pear.</b>","hi":"नींबू सिट्रस कुल का फल है<br>उसी प्रकार उत्तर Rosaceae कुल का फल होना चाहिए, और नाशपाती गुलाब कुल की है ✔<br>हिबिस्कस मालो कुल का तथा आम काजू कुल का है, जबकि क्लियोपेट्रा कोई पौधा नहीं है<br>इसलिए उत्तर Pear है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): नाशपाती है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000069996","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"In the following question, select the related word from the given alternatives.<br>WORD : ULMW :: PLAY : ? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में दिए गए विकल्पों में से संबंधित शब्द चुनिए।<br>WORD : ULMW :: PLAY : ? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"NOUB"},"2":{"en":"OGVR"},"3":{"en":"MIU"},"4":{"en":"NIVR"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The letters of WORD move back by the prime numbers 2, 3, 5 and 7 in order: W&#8594;U (−2), O&#8594;L (−3), R&#8594;M (−5) and D&#8594;W (−7, counting back past A) ✔<br>Applying the same steps to PLAY: P&#8594;N (−2), L&#8594;I (−3), A&#8594;V (−5) and Y&#8594;R (−7)<br>Hence PLAY is coded as NIVR<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): NIVR.</b>","hi":"WORD के अक्षर क्रमशः अभाज्य संख्याओं 2, 3, 5 तथा 7 के बराबर पीछे जाते हैं: W&#8594;U (−2), O&#8594;L (−3), R&#8594;M (−5) तथा D&#8594;W (−7, A से पीछे गिनते हुए) ✔<br>PLAY पर वही चरण लगाने से P&#8594;N (−2), L&#8594;I (−3), A&#8594;V (−5) तथा Y&#8594;R (−7)<br>इसलिए PLAY का कूट NIVR है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): NIVR है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000069997","section":"REASONING","topic":"Odd One Out","question":{"en":"Which of the following is different from the rest? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा शेष से भिन्न है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4"},"2":{"en":"16"},"3":{"en":"25"},"4":{"en":"36"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"4 = 2², 16 = 4² and 36 = 6² are squares of even numbers<br>25 = 5² is the square of an odd number, so it is different from the rest<br>Hence 25 is different<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 25.</b>","hi":"4 = 2², 16 = 4² तथा 36 = 6² सम संख्याओं के वर्ग हैं<br>25 = 5² विषम संख्या का वर्ग है, अतः यह शेष से भिन्न है<br>इसलिए 25 भिन्न है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 25 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000069998","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Formation & Letter/Word Position","question":{"en":"Which meaningful word can be formed from the letters \"NOMRECEY\"? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"अक्षरों \"NOMRECEY\" से कौन-सा अर्थपूर्ण शब्द बनाया जा सकता है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"NOMERCY"},"2":{"en":"CEROMNY"},"3":{"en":"CEREMONY"},"4":{"en":"NOMERECY"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The given letters are N, O, M, R, E, C, E and Y, that is one N, one M, one R, two E, one C, one O and one Y<br>CEREMONY needs exactly the letters C, E, R, E, M, O, N, Y, which are all present in the required numbers ✔<br>The other options are not meaningful English words<br>Hence CEREMONY is the word that can be formed<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): CEREMONY.</b>","hi":"दिए गए अक्षर N, O, M, R, E, C, E तथा Y हैं, अर्थात् एक N, एक M, एक R, दो E, एक C, एक O तथा एक Y<br>CEREMONY के लिए C, E, R, E, M, O, N, Y अक्षर चाहिए, जो सभी आवश्यक संख्या में उपलब्ध हैं ✔<br>अन्य विकल्प अर्थपूर्ण अंग्रेज़ी शब्द नहीं हैं<br>इसलिए CEREMONY वह शब्द है जो बनाया जा सकता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): CEREMONY है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000069999","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"Find the 10th term of the AP.<br>2.5, 3.0, 3.5, ... [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"समांतर श्रेणी का 10वाँ पद ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>2.5, 3.0, 3.5, ... [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6.5"},"2":{"en":"7.0"},"3":{"en":"6.0"},"4":{"en":"5.5"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The first term is a = 2.5 and the common difference is d = 3.0 − 2.5 = 0.5<br>The nth term is a + (n − 1)d, so the 10th term is 2.5 + 9 × 0.5 = 2.5 + 4.5 = 7.0<br>Hence the 10th term is 7.0<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 7.0.</b>","hi":"पहला पद a = 2.5 तथा सार्व अंतर d = 3.0 − 2.5 = 0.5 है<br>nवाँ पद a + (n − 1)d है, अतः 10वाँ पद 2.5 + 9 × 0.5 = 2.5 + 4.5 = 7.0 है<br>इसलिए 10वाँ पद 7.0 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 7.0 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000070000","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"If PLANT is coded as QMBOU, how is QMBOU coded? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि PLANT का कूट QMBOU है, तो QMBOU का कूट क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"RNCOV"},"2":{"en":"RNBOU"},"3":{"en":"RNCPV"},"4":{"en":"QMBOV"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In PLANT each letter moves one place ahead: P→Q, L→M, A→B, N→O and T→U, which gives QMBOU ✔<br>Applying the same step to QMBOU: Q→R, M→N, B→C, O→P and U→V<br>Hence QMBOU is coded as RNCPV<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): RNCPV.</b>","hi":"PLANT में प्रत्येक अक्षर एक स्थान आगे जाता है: P→Q, L→M, A→B, N→O तथा T→U, जिससे QMBOU मिलता है ✔<br>QMBOU पर वही चरण लगाने से Q→R, M→N, B→C, O→P तथा U→V<br>इसलिए QMBOU का कूट RNCPV है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): RNCPV है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000070001","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"INDEPENDENCE\" is written as \"JNEEQEODFNDE\". How will \"REPRESENTATION\" be written? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"INDEPENDENCE\" को \"JNEEQEODFNDE\" लिखा जाता है। \"REPRESENTATION\" कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"SEQRFSFNUAUIPN"},"2":{"en":"SEQRSFFNUAUIPN"},"3":{"en":"SEQRFSNAUFUIPN"},"4":{"en":"SEQRSFFNUAIUPN"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Step 1: Number the letters of INDEPENDENCE and compare with its code</b><br>INDEPENDENCE → JNEEQEODFNDE<br>1. I → J (+1)<br>2. N → N (same)<br>3. D → E (+1)<br>4. E → E (same)<br>5. P → Q (+1)<br>6. E → E (same)<br>7. N → O (+1)<br>8. D → D (same)<br>9. E → F (+1)<br>10. N → N (same)<br>11. C → D (+1)<br>12. E → E (same)<br><br><b>Step 2: Find the rule</b><br>The letters at the <b>odd</b> positions (1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11) move <b>one place forward</b> in the alphabet.<br>The letters at the <b>even</b> positions (2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12) stay <b>the same</b>.<br><br><b>Step 3: Number the letters of REPRESENTATION</b><br>R(1) E(2) P(3) R(4) E(5) S(6) E(7) N(8) T(9) A(10) T(11) I(12) O(13) N(14)<br><br><b>Step 4: Apply the rule</b><br>1. R (odd) → S<br>2. E (even) → E<br>3. P (odd) → Q<br>4. R (even) → R<br>5. E (odd) → F<br>6. S (even) → S<br>7. E (odd) → F<br>8. N (even) → N<br>9. T (odd) → U<br>10. A (even) → A<br>11. T (odd) → U<br>12. I (even) → I<br>13. O (odd) → P<br>14. N (even) → N<br><br><b>Step 5: Join the letters</b><br>S + E + Q + R + F + S + F + N + U + A + U + I + P + N = <b>SEQRFSFNUAUIPN</b><br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): SEQRFSFNUAUIPN.</b>","hi":"<b>चरण 1: INDEPENDENCE के अक्षरों को क्रमांकित करें और उसके कूट से तुलना करें</b><br>INDEPENDENCE → JNEEQEODFNDE<br>1. I → J (+1)<br>2. N → N (वैसा)<br>3. D → E (+1)<br>4. E → E (वैसा)<br>5. P → Q (+1)<br>6. E → E (वैसा)<br>7. N → O (+1)<br>8. D → D (वैसा)<br>9. E → F (+1)<br>10. N → N (वैसा)<br>11. C → D (+1)<br>12. E → E (वैसा)<br><br><b>चरण 2: नियम ज्ञात करें</b><br><b>विषम</b> स्थानों (1, 3, 5, 7, 9, 11) के अक्षर वर्णमाला में <b>एक स्थान आगे</b> बढ़ते हैं।<br><b>सम</b> स्थानों (2, 4, 6, 8, 10, 12) के अक्षर <b>वैसे ही</b> रहते हैं।<br><br><b>चरण 3: REPRESENTATION के अक्षरों को क्रमांकित करें</b><br>R(1) E(2) P(3) R(4) E(5) S(6) E(7) N(8) T(9) A(10) T(11) I(12) O(13) N(14)<br><br><b>चरण 4: नियम लगाएँ</b><br>1. R (विषम) → S<br>2. E (सम) → E<br>3. P (विषम) → Q<br>4. R (सम) → R<br>5. E (विषम) → F<br>6. S (सम) → S<br>7. E (विषम) → F<br>8. N (सम) → N<br>9. T (विषम) → U<br>10. A (सम) → A<br>11. T (विषम) → U<br>12. I (सम) → I<br>13. O (विषम) → P<br>14. N (सम) → N<br><br><b>चरण 5: अक्षरों को जोड़ें</b><br>S + E + Q + R + F + S + F + N + U + A + U + I + P + N = <b>SEQRFSFNUAUIPN</b><br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): SEQRFSFNUAUIPN है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000070002","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">22</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">44</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">36</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">28</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">24</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">32</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। यह पैटर्न पहचानिए और उसके अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">22</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">44</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">36</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">28</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">24</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">6</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">16</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">12</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">32</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"18"},"2":{"en":"34"},"3":{"en":"24"},"4":{"en":"40"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The third row is 6, 16, 12 and the fourth row is exactly double it: 12 = 2 × 6, 32 = 2 × 16 and therefore the third entry is 2 × 12 = 24 ✔<br>The same check works in the other rows because the sum of the first two entries of a row and its third entry always keep the ratio 11 : 6: 66 and 36 in row one, 44 and 24 in row two, 22 and 12 in row three and 44 and 24 in row four<br>Both readings give the same value for the missing entry<br>Hence the missing number is 24<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 24.</b>","hi":"तीसरी पंक्ति 6, 16, 12 है और चौथी पंक्ति ठीक उसकी दो गुनी है: 12 = 2 × 6, 32 = 2 × 16 और इसलिए तीसरा पद 2 × 12 = 24 है ✔<br>अन्य पंक्तियों में भी यही जाँच लगती है, क्योंकि पंक्ति के पहले दो पदों का योग तथा तीसरा पद सदैव 11 : 6 अनुपात में हैं: पहली पंक्ति में 66 और 36, दूसरी में 44 और 24, तीसरी में 22 और 12 तथा चौथी में 44 और 24<br>दोनों प्रकार से लुप्त पद का वही मान मिलता है<br>इसलिए लुप्त संख्या 24 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 24 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000070003","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"If M + N means M is the husband of N; M - N means M is the sister of N; M * N means M is the son of N, what does A * B - C + D mean? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि M + N का अर्थ है M, N का पति है; M - N का अर्थ है M, N की बहन है; M * N का अर्थ है M, N का पुत्र है, तो A * B - C + D का क्या अर्थ है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A is the son of C's husband.","hi":"A, C के पति का पुत्र है।"},"2":{"en":"A is the brother of C.","hi":"A, C का भाई है।"},"3":{"en":"A is the grandson of D.","hi":"A, D का पौत्र है।"},"4":{"en":"A is the nephew of C.","hi":"A, C का भांजा है।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"A * B means A is the son of B<br>B - C means B is the sister of C, so B and C are siblings and A is the child of C's sister<br>C + D means C is the husband of D<br>Since A is the son of C's sister, A is the nephew of C<br>Hence A * B - C + D means A is the nephew of C<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): A is the nephew of C..</b>","hi":"A * B का अर्थ है A, B का पुत्र है<br>B - C का अर्थ है B, C की बहन है, अतः B तथा C सहोदर हैं और A, C की बहन की संतान है<br>C + D का अर्थ है C, D का पति है<br>चूँकि A, C की बहन का पुत्र है, अतः A, C का भांजा है<br>इसलिए A * B - C + D का अर्थ है A, C का भांजा है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): A, C का भांजा है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000070004","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"You have a brilliant subordinate who produces the highest quality work in the office. However, their internal need for perfection is so high that they regularly miss project deadlines by days, causing the entire department to scramble. When you point this out, they break down, saying their self-worth is entirely tied to the \"perfection\" of their output and that any compromise feels like a \"personal failure.\" What is the most structurally sound intervention? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"आपके पास एक प्रतिभाशाली अधीनस्थ है जो कार्यालय में सर्वोच्च गुणवत्ता का कार्य करता है। परंतु उसकी पूर्णता की आंतरिक आवश्यकता इतनी अधिक है कि वह नियमित रूप से परियोजना की समय-सीमा कई दिन चूक जाता है, जिससे पूरा विभाग परेशान हो जाता है। जब आप यह बताते हैं, तो वह टूट जाता है और कहता है कि उसका आत्म-मूल्य पूरी तरह उसके कार्य की \"पूर्णता\" से जुड़ा है और कोई भी समझौता उसे \"व्यक्तिगत असफलता\" लगता है। सर्वाधिक उपयुक्त हस्तक्षेप क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Tell them that they must stop being a perfectionist or they will be fired, as business requires speed.","hi":"उन्हें बताएँ कि उन्हें पूर्णतावादी बनना बंद करना होगा वरना नौकरी से निकाल दिया जाएगा, क्योंकि व्यवसाय को गति चाहिए।"},"2":{"en":"Acknowledge their perfectionism and define realistic quality thresholds for each project stage.","hi":"उनके पूर्णतावाद को स्वीकार करें और परियोजना के प्रत्येक चरण के लिए व्यावहारिक गुणवत्ता मानक तय करें।"},"3":{"en":"Reduce their workload by 50% so they have more time to perfect the few tasks they do receive.","hi":"उनका कार्यभार 50% घटा दें ताकि उनके पास मिले कुछ कार्यों को पूर्ण करने का अधिक समय हो।"},"4":{"en":"Stop giving them any deadlines so they can work at their own pace without stress.","hi":"उन्हें कोई समय-सीमा देना बंद कर दें ताकि वे बिना तनाव के अपनी गति से काम कर सकें।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The real problem is that the person has no agreed standard of what is good enough, so every task keeps getting polished and the deadline slips<br>Fixing clear and realistic quality thresholds for each stage gives the person a target that can be met and keeps self-worth separate from endless polishing<br>Threatening the job or removing all deadlines avoids the issue, and cutting the workload in half does not change the habit and shifts the burden to others<br>Hence acknowledging the perfectionism and defining realistic quality thresholds is the sound intervention<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Acknowledge their perfectionism and define realistic quality thresholds for each project stage..</b>","hi":"वास्तविक समस्या यह है कि व्यक्ति के पास इस बात का तय मानक नहीं है कि कितना अच्छा पर्याप्त है, अतः हर कार्य पर सुधार चलता रहता है और समय-सीमा चूक जाती है<br>प्रत्येक चरण के लिए स्पष्ट तथा व्यावहारिक गुणवत्ता मानक तय करने से व्यक्ति को प्राप्त करने योग्य लक्ष्य मिलता है और आत्म-मूल्य अनंत सुधार से अलग हो जाता है<br>नौकरी की धमकी या सभी समय-सीमाएँ हटा देना समस्या से बचना है, और कार्यभार आधा करना आदत नहीं बदलता तथा भार दूसरों पर डाल देता है<br>इसलिए पूर्णतावाद को स्वीकार करके व्यावहारिक गुणवत्ता मानक तय करना उपयुक्त हस्तक्षेप है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): उनके पूर्णतावाद को स्वीकार करें और परियोजना के प्रत्येक चरण के लिए व्यावहारिक गुणवत्ता मानक तय करें। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000070005","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"To manage the increasing energy demand in the city, the local council has proposed providing substantial subsidies to residents who install solar panels on their rooftops. Which of the following assumptions underlies the argument for providing these subsidies? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"शहर की बढ़ती ऊर्जा माँग को संभालने के लिए स्थानीय परिषद ने छतों पर सौर पैनल लगाने वाले निवासियों को पर्याप्त सब्सिडी देने का प्रस्ताव रखा है। इन सब्सिडी के पक्ष में तर्क के पीछे निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सी अवधारणा निहित है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Providing financial incentives for solar adoption is the only way to meet future energy demands.","hi":"सौर ऊर्जा अपनाने के लिए वित्तीय प्रोत्साहन देना भविष्य की ऊर्जा माँग पूरी करने का एकमात्र उपाय है।"},"2":{"en":"The current infrastructure is entirely unable to support the city's growing energy consumption.","hi":"वर्तमान अवसंरचना शहर की बढ़ती ऊर्जा खपत को सहारा देने में पूरी तरह असमर्थ है।"},"3":{"en":"Financial costs are a significant barrier to residents adopting solar technology.","hi":"निवासियों के लिए वित्तीय लागत सौर प्रौद्योगिकी अपनाने में एक बड़ी बाधा है।"},"4":{"en":"Solar panels installed on residential rooftops will eliminate the need for power plants.","hi":"घरों की छतों पर लगे सौर पैनल बिजलीघरों की आवश्यकता समाप्त कर देंगे।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"A subsidy works as a reason for action only when money is what holds people back, so the argument assumes that the cost of solar panels is a real barrier for residents<br>The first option makes the subsidy the only way, the second calls the present set-up entirely unable and the fourth says power plants will not be needed, all of which are extreme and not needed for the argument<br>Hence the assumption is that financial costs are a significant barrier to residents adopting solar technology<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Financial costs are a significant barrier to residents adopting solar technology..</b>","hi":"सब्सिडी तभी कारण बनती है जब पैसा ही लोगों को रोक रहा हो, अतः तर्क यह मानता है कि सौर पैनल की लागत निवासियों के लिए वास्तविक बाधा है<br>पहला विकल्प सब्सिडी को एकमात्र उपाय बताता है, दूसरा वर्तमान व्यवस्था को पूरी तरह असमर्थ कहता है और चौथा कहता है कि बिजलीघरों की आवश्यकता नहीं रहेगी, जो सभी अत्यधिक हैं और तर्क के लिए आवश्यक नहीं<br>इसलिए अवधारणा यह है कि वित्तीय लागत सौर प्रौद्योगिकी अपनाने में एक बड़ी बाधा है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): निवासियों के लिए वित्तीय लागत सौर प्रौद्योगिकी अपनाने में एक बड़ी बाधा है। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000070006","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Reports and Indices","question":{"en":"Which high-level global metric predominantly derives its evaluation of subjective well-being from data collected through the Gallup World Poll? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कौन-सा उच्च-स्तरीय वैश्विक मापक मुख्य रूप से गैलप वर्ल्ड पोल (Gallup World Poll) के माध्यम से एकत्रित आँकड़ों से व्यक्तिपरक कल्याण (subjective well-being) का मूल्यांकन करता है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"World Happiness Index","hi":"विश्व प्रसन्नता सूचकांक"},"2":{"en":"Global Competitiveness Index","hi":"वैश्विक प्रतिस्पर्धात्मकता सूचकांक"},"3":{"en":"Environmental Performance Index","hi":"पर्यावरण प्रदर्शन सूचकांक"},"4":{"en":"Human Development Index","hi":"मानव विकास सूचकांक"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – World Happiness Index</b><br>The <b>World Happiness Report</b> ranks countries on life evaluations taken from the <b><u>Gallup World Poll</u></b>, where people rate their own lives on the Cantril ladder (0–10).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Published by the <b>UN Sustainable Development Solutions Network</b> with Gallup and Oxford Wellbeing Research Centre; first released in <b>2012</b>.<br>• <b>Finland</b> has topped the report for several consecutive years.<br>• Global Competitiveness Index – <b>World Economic Forum</b>; HDI – <b>UNDP</b>; Environmental Performance Index – <b>Yale and Columbia Universities</b>.<br>• 20 March is observed as the <b>International Day of Happiness</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – विश्व प्रसन्नता सूचकांक</b><br><b>विश्व प्रसन्नता रिपोर्ट (World Happiness Report)</b> देशों को <b><u>गैलप वर्ल्ड पोल (Gallup World Poll)</u></b> से लिए गए जीवन-मूल्यांकन के आधार पर रैंक करती है, जिसमें लोग कैंट्रिल सीढ़ी (Cantril ladder, 0–10) पर अपने जीवन को अंक देते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>संयुक्त राष्ट्र सतत विकास समाधान नेटवर्क (UN SDSN)</b> द्वारा गैलप और ऑक्सफोर्ड वेलबीइंग रिसर्च सेंटर के साथ प्रकाशित; पहली बार <b>2012</b> में जारी।<br>• <b>फ़िनलैंड (Finland)</b> लगातार कई वर्षों से इस रिपोर्ट में शीर्ष पर है।<br>• वैश्विक प्रतिस्पर्धात्मकता सूचकांक – <b>विश्व आर्थिक मंच (WEF)</b>; मानव विकास सूचकांक – <b>UNDP</b>; पर्यावरण प्रदर्शन सूचकांक – <b>येल और कोलंबिया विश्वविद्यालय</b>।<br>• 20 मार्च को <b>अंतर्राष्ट्रीय प्रसन्नता दिवस (International Day of Happiness)</b> मनाया जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000070007","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Reports and Indices","question":{"en":"What is a key goal of the Human Development Index (HDI)? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"मानव विकास सूचकांक (HDI) का एक प्रमुख लक्ष्य क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To shift the focus from solely economic development to human development.","hi":"केवल आर्थिक विकास से ध्यान हटाकर मानव विकास पर केंद्रित करना।"},"2":{"en":"To only measure economic growth.","hi":"केवल आर्थिक संवृद्धि को मापना।"},"3":{"en":"To only measure military strength.","hi":"केवल सैन्य शक्ति को मापना।"},"4":{"en":"To only measure environmental impact.","hi":"केवल पर्यावरणीय प्रभाव को मापना।"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – To shift the focus from solely economic development to human development.</b><br>HDI was designed to show that <b>people and their capabilities</b>, not economic growth alone, should be the <b><u>ultimate criterion</u></b> for judging the development of a country.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Developed by <b>Mahbub ul Haq</b> (with Amartya Sen); first published by <b>UNDP in 1990</b>.<br>• Three dimensions: <b>long and healthy life</b> (life expectancy), <b>knowledge</b> (years of schooling) and <b>decent standard of living</b> (GNI per capita, PPP).<br>• HDI is the <b>geometric mean</b> of the three dimension indices; value ranges from 0 to 1.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – केवल आर्थिक विकास से ध्यान हटाकर मानव विकास पर केंद्रित करना।</b><br>HDI यह दिखाने के लिए बनाया गया कि किसी देश के विकास को आँकने का <b><u>अंतिम मानदंड</u></b> केवल आर्थिक संवृद्धि नहीं, बल्कि <b>लोग और उनकी क्षमताएँ</b> होनी चाहिए।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>महबूब-उल-हक (Mahbub ul Haq)</b> ने (अमर्त्य सेन के साथ) विकसित किया; पहली बार <b>1990 में UNDP</b> द्वारा प्रकाशित।<br>• तीन आयाम: <b>दीर्घ और स्वस्थ जीवन</b> (जीवन प्रत्याशा), <b>ज्ञान</b> (स्कूली शिक्षा के वर्ष) और <b>उचित जीवन स्तर</b> (प्रति व्यक्ति GNI, PPP)।<br>• HDI तीनों आयाम सूचकांकों का <b>गुणोत्तर माध्य (Geometric mean)</b> है; इसका मान 0 से 1 के बीच होता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000070008","section":"GK","topic":"Environment: Basics of Environmental Sciences","question":{"en":"How many categories does the USA Air Quality Index (AQI) use to classify air quality? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"संयुक्त राज्य अमेरिका का वायु गुणवत्ता सूचकांक (AQI) वायु गुणवत्ता को वर्गीकृत करने के लिए कितनी श्रेणियों का उपयोग करता है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4"},"2":{"en":"5"},"3":{"en":"6"},"4":{"en":"8"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 6</b><br>The US EPA's AQI uses <b><u>six categories</u></b>, each with its own colour code, on a scale of 0 to 500.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• US categories: Good (green), Moderate (yellow), Unhealthy for Sensitive Groups (orange), Unhealthy (red), Very Unhealthy (purple), Hazardous (maroon).<br>• India's <b>National AQI</b> was launched in <b>2014</b> by CPCB and also has <b>six categories</b> (Good to Severe).<br>• Indian AQI considers <b>eight pollutants</b>: PM10, PM2.5, NO₂, SO₂, CO, O₃, NH₃ and Pb.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 6</b><br>अमेरिकी EPA का AQI 0 से 500 के पैमाने पर <b><u>छह श्रेणियों</u></b> का उपयोग करता है, जिनमें से प्रत्येक का अपना रंग कोड है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अमेरिकी श्रेणियाँ: अच्छा (हरा), मध्यम (पीला), संवेदनशील समूहों के लिए अस्वास्थ्यकर (नारंगी), अस्वास्थ्यकर (लाल), बहुत अस्वास्थ्यकर (बैंगनी), खतरनाक (मैरून)।<br>• भारत का <b>राष्ट्रीय AQI (National AQI)</b> <b>2014</b> में CPCB द्वारा शुरू किया गया; इसमें भी <b>छह श्रेणियाँ</b> (अच्छा से गंभीर) हैं।<br>• भारतीय AQI <b>आठ प्रदूषकों</b> को ध्यान में रखता है: PM10, PM2.5, NO₂, SO₂, CO, O₃, NH₃ और Pb।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000070009","section":"GK","topic":"Science and Technology: Science and Technology","question":{"en":"Which of the following satellites is launched by ISRO for disaster management and natural resource monitoring? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा उपग्रह इसरो (ISRO) द्वारा आपदा प्रबंधन और प्राकृतिक संसाधन निगरानी के लिए प्रक्षेपित किया गया है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Astrosat","hi":"एस्ट्रोसैट"},"2":{"en":"GSAT","hi":"जीसैट"},"3":{"en":"RISAT","hi":"रीसैट"},"4":{"en":"Cartosat","hi":"कार्टोसैट"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – RISAT</b><br><b>RISAT (Radar Imaging Satellite)</b> carries a <b><u>Synthetic Aperture Radar</u></b> that images the Earth day and night in all weather, making it useful for floods, cyclones, agriculture and forest monitoring.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>RISAT-2</b> was launched in 2009 and <b>RISAT-1</b> (first indigenous radar imaging satellite) in 2012.<br>• <b>Astrosat</b> (2015) – India's first dedicated multi-wavelength space observatory.<br>• <b>GSAT</b> – communication satellites; <b>Cartosat</b> – high-resolution cartography (mapping) satellites.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – रीसैट</b><br><b>रीसैट (Radar Imaging Satellite)</b> में <b><u>सिंथेटिक अपर्चर रडार (Synthetic Aperture Radar)</u></b> लगा है, जो हर मौसम में दिन-रात पृथ्वी की तस्वीरें लेता है; इसलिए यह बाढ़, चक्रवात, कृषि और वन निगरानी में उपयोगी है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>RISAT-2</b> 2009 में तथा <b>RISAT-1</b> (पहला स्वदेशी रडार इमेजिंग उपग्रह) 2012 में प्रक्षेपित।<br>• <b>एस्ट्रोसैट (Astrosat)</b> (2015) – भारत की पहली समर्पित बहु-तरंगदैर्ध्य अंतरिक्ष वेधशाला।<br>• <b>जीसैट (GSAT)</b> – संचार उपग्रह; <b>कार्टोसैट (Cartosat)</b> – उच्च-विभेदन मानचित्रण (Cartography) उपग्रह।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000070010","section":"GK","topic":"Science and Technology: Science and Technology","question":{"en":"Which technology is ISRO testing through the RLV-TD project? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"इसरो RLV-TD परियोजना के माध्यम से किस प्रौद्योगिकी का परीक्षण कर रहा है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Robotic lunar excavation","hi":"रोबोटिक चंद्र उत्खनन"},"2":{"en":"Underwater satellite deployment","hi":"जल के भीतर उपग्रह तैनाती"},"3":{"en":"Deep space communication","hi":"गहन अंतरिक्ष संचार"},"4":{"en":"Reusable space launch vehicles","hi":"पुन: प्रयोज्य अंतरिक्ष प्रक्षेपण यान"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Reusable space launch vehicles</b><br>RLV-TD stands for <b>Reusable Launch Vehicle – Technology Demonstrator</b>. It tests the technologies needed for a <b><u>reusable launch vehicle</u></b> that can cut the cost of access to space.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• First flight test <b>RLV-TD HEX-01</b> was conducted in <b>May 2016</b> from Sriharikota.<br>• Autonomous landing experiments (<b>RLV-LEX</b>) were carried out at the <b>Aeronautical Test Range, Chitradurga (Karnataka)</b> in 2023–24; the vehicle is named <b>Pushpak</b>.<br>• ISRO HQ: <b>Bengaluru</b>; founded in <b>1969</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – पुन: प्रयोज्य अंतरिक्ष प्रक्षेपण यान</b><br>RLV-TD का पूर्ण रूप <b>पुन: प्रयोज्य प्रक्षेपण यान – प्रौद्योगिकी प्रदर्शक (Reusable Launch Vehicle – Technology Demonstrator)</b> है। यह <b><u>पुन: प्रयोज्य प्रक्षेपण यान</u></b> के लिए आवश्यक तकनीकों का परीक्षण करता है, जिससे अंतरिक्ष तक पहुँच की लागत घटे।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पहला उड़ान परीक्षण <b>RLV-TD HEX-01</b> <b>मई 2016</b> में श्रीहरिकोटा से किया गया।<br>• स्वायत्त लैंडिंग प्रयोग (<b>RLV-LEX</b>) 2023–24 में <b>एयरोनॉटिकल टेस्ट रेंज, चित्रदुर्ग (कर्नाटक)</b> में किए गए; यान का नाम <b>पुष्पक</b> है।<br>• इसरो मुख्यालय: <b>बेंगलुरु</b>; स्थापना <b>1969</b> में।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000070011","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: The Mughal Empire","question":{"en":"The construction of Taj Mahal was completed in which year? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"ताजमहल का निर्माण किस वर्ष पूरा हुआ था? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1631"},"2":{"en":"1643"},"3":{"en":"1653"},"4":{"en":"1666"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 1653</b><br>The <b>Taj Mahal</b> was built by <b>Shah Jahan</b> in memory of Mumtaz Mahal. Work began in 1632 and the whole complex was completed in <b><u>1653</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Chief architect: <b>Ustad Ahmad Lahauri</b>; built on the bank of the <b>Yamuna</b> at Agra.<br>• Declared a <b>UNESCO World Heritage Site in 1983</b>.<br>• Mumtaz Mahal died in <b>1631</b>; Shah Jahan also built the <b>Red Fort</b> and <b>Jama Masjid</b> in Delhi.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 1653</b><br><b>ताजमहल</b> का निर्माण <b>शाहजहाँ</b> ने मुमताज़ महल की स्मृति में करवाया। कार्य 1632 में शुरू हुआ और पूरा परिसर <b><u>1653</u></b> में बनकर तैयार हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मुख्य वास्तुकार: <b>उस्ताद अहमद लाहौरी</b>; आगरा में <b>यमुना</b> के तट पर निर्मित।<br>• <b>1983 में यूनेस्को विश्व धरोहर स्थल (UNESCO World Heritage Site)</b> घोषित।<br>• मुमताज़ महल की मृत्यु <b>1631</b> में हुई; शाहजहाँ ने दिल्ली में <b>लाल किला</b> और <b>जामा मस्जिद</b> भी बनवाई।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000070012","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: International Organisations","question":{"en":"What is a key aspect of the Quad's (Quadrilateral Security Dialogue) approach to regional security? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"क्षेत्रीय सुरक्षा के प्रति क्वाड (चतुर्पक्षीय सुरक्षा संवाद) के दृष्टिकोण का एक प्रमुख पहलू क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Forming a formal military alliance","hi":"एक औपचारिक सैन्य गठबंधन बनाना"},"2":{"en":"Promoting multilateral cooperation","hi":"बहुपक्षीय सहयोग को बढ़ावा देना"},"3":{"en":"Isolating regional powers","hi":"क्षेत्रीय शक्तियों को अलग-थलग करना"},"4":{"en":"Creating exclusive trade blocs","hi":"विशिष्ट व्यापार गुट बनाना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Promoting multilateral cooperation</b><br>The Quad is an <b>informal strategic forum</b>, not a military alliance. It works through <b><u>multilateral cooperation</u></b> for a free, open and inclusive Indo-Pacific.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Members: <b>India, USA, Japan and Australia</b>.<br>• Idea emerged after the <b>2004 Indian Ocean tsunami</b>; first formal talks in <b>2007</b>, revived in <b>2017</b>.<br>• First leaders' summit (virtual) was held in <b>March 2021</b>; the Quad has no permanent secretariat.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – बहुपक्षीय सहयोग को बढ़ावा देना</b><br>क्वाड एक <b>अनौपचारिक रणनीतिक मंच</b> है, सैन्य गठबंधन नहीं। यह स्वतंत्र, खुले और समावेशी हिंद-प्रशांत के लिए <b><u>बहुपक्षीय सहयोग (Multilateral cooperation)</u></b> के माध्यम से कार्य करता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सदस्य: <b>भारत, अमेरिका, जापान और ऑस्ट्रेलिया</b>।<br>• विचार <b>2004 की हिंद महासागर सुनामी</b> के बाद उभरा; पहली औपचारिक वार्ता <b>2007</b> में, <b>2017</b> में पुनर्जीवित।<br>• पहला नेता-स्तरीय शिखर सम्मेलन (वर्चुअल) <b>मार्च 2021</b> में हुआ; क्वाड का कोई स्थायी सचिवालय नहीं है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000070013","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"How many points are awarded for a successful \"touchdown\" in American Football? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"अमेरिकी फ़ुटबॉल में सफल \"टचडाउन\" के लिए कितने अंक दिए जाते हैं? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3"},"2":{"en":"5"},"3":{"en":"6"},"4":{"en":"7"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 6</b><br>A <b>touchdown</b>, scored by carrying or catching the ball in the opponent's end zone, is worth <b><u>6 points</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• After a touchdown, a kick (extra point) gives <b>1 point</b> and a two-point conversion gives <b>2 points</b>.<br>• A <b>field goal</b> = 3 points; a <b>safety</b> = 2 points.<br>• The NFL championship game is called the <b>Super Bowl</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 6</b><br>विरोधी के एंड ज़ोन (End zone) में गेंद ले जाकर या पकड़कर किया गया <b>टचडाउन (Touchdown)</b> <b><u>6 अंक</u></b> का होता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• टचडाउन के बाद किक (अतिरिक्त अंक) से <b>1 अंक</b> और टू-पॉइंट कन्वर्ज़न से <b>2 अंक</b> मिलते हैं।<br>• <b>फ़ील्ड गोल (Field goal)</b> = 3 अंक; <b>सेफ्टी (Safety)</b> = 2 अंक।<br>• NFL के चैंपियनशिप मैच को <b>सुपर बाउल (Super Bowl)</b> कहते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000070014","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Post-Maurya Dynasties","question":{"en":"Which part of early Gandhara art shows that it was influenced by Greek art styles? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"प्रारंभिक गांधार कला का कौन-सा भाग दर्शाता है कि वह यूनानी कला शैलियों से प्रभावित थी? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Symbolic representation of Buddha through footprints","hi":"पदचिह्नों के माध्यम से बुद्ध का प्रतीकात्मक चित्रण"},"2":{"en":"Use of terracotta in religious art","hi":"धार्मिक कला में टेराकोटा का उपयोग"},"3":{"en":"Depiction of the Buddha with draped robe and wavy hair","hi":"लहराते वस्त्र और घुंघराले बालों के साथ बुद्ध का चित्रण"},"4":{"en":"Use of floral capitals and bell-shaped domes","hi":"पुष्पीय शीर्ष और घंटाकार गुंबदों का उपयोग"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Depiction of the Buddha with draped robe and wavy hair</b><br>Gandhara sculptures show the Buddha in a <b>Greco-Roman (Hellenistic)</b> style – with <b><u>heavy draped robes, wavy/curly hair</u></b> and realistic, muscular features like Apollo.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Flourished under the <b>Kushanas</b>, especially <b>Kanishka</b>; mainly used <b>grey/blue-grey schist</b> stone.<br>• <b>Mathura school</b> – indigenous style using <b>red sandstone</b>; <b>Amaravati school</b> – white marble, patronised by Satavahanas.<br>• Symbolic representation of the Buddha (footprints, wheel, Bodhi tree) belongs to <b>early Buddhist (pre-Kushana) art</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – लहराते वस्त्र और घुंघराले बालों के साथ बुद्ध का चित्रण</b><br>गांधार मूर्तियाँ बुद्ध को <b>यूनानी-रोमन (Hellenistic)</b> शैली में दिखाती हैं – <b><u>भारी लहराते वस्त्र, घुंघराले बाल</u></b> और अपोलो जैसी यथार्थवादी, मांसल आकृति के साथ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>कुषाणों</b>, विशेषकर <b>कनिष्क</b> के संरक्षण में फली-फूली; मुख्यतः <b>धूसर/नीले-धूसर शिस्ट (Schist)</b> पत्थर का उपयोग।<br>• <b>मथुरा शैली</b> – <b>लाल बलुआ पत्थर</b> वाली स्वदेशी शैली; <b>अमरावती शैली</b> – सफेद संगमरमर, सातवाहनों द्वारा संरक्षित।<br>• पदचिह्न, चक्र, बोधि वृक्ष द्वारा बुद्ध का प्रतीकात्मक चित्रण <b>प्रारंभिक बौद्ध (पूर्व-कुषाण) कला</b> की विशेषता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000070015","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Books and Authors","question":{"en":"Who won the 1976 Booker Prize for “Heat and Dust,” a novel that juxtaposes colonial India with postcolonial experiences? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"औपनिवेशिक भारत और उत्तर-औपनिवेशिक अनुभवों की तुलना करने वाले उपन्यास “हीट एंड डस्ट” के लिए 1976 का बुकर पुरस्कार किसने जीता? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Salman Rushdie","hi":"सलमान रुश्दी"},"2":{"en":"J.G. Farrell","hi":"जे.जी. फैरेल"},"3":{"en":"Ruth Prawer Jhabvala","hi":"रूथ प्रावर झाबवाला"},"4":{"en":"Anita Desai","hi":"अनीता देसाई"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Ruth Prawer Jhabvala</b><br><b>Ruth Prawer Jhabvala</b> won the Booker Prize for <b><u>“Heat and Dust”</u></b>, which links the 1920s story of Olivia with her step-granddaughter's journey in 1970s India.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Note:</b> Heat and Dust won the Booker Prize of <b>1975</b> (book published 1975).<br>• <b>Salman Rushdie</b> won the Booker in 1981 for <b>Midnight's Children</b>.<br>• <b>J.G. Farrell</b> won in 1973 for <b>The Siege of Krishnapur</b>; <b>Anita Desai</b> was shortlisted three times.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – रूथ प्रावर झाबवाला</b><br><b>रूथ प्रावर झाबवाला</b> ने <b><u>“हीट एंड डस्ट (Heat and Dust)”</u></b> के लिए बुकर पुरस्कार जीता, जो 1920 के दशक की ओलिविया की कहानी को 1970 के दशक में भारत आई उसकी सौतेली पोती की यात्रा से जोड़ता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>नोट:</b> हीट एंड डस्ट ने <b>1975</b> का बुकर पुरस्कार जीता था (पुस्तक 1975 में प्रकाशित)।<br>• <b>सलमान रुश्दी</b> ने 1981 में <b>मिडनाइट्स चिल्ड्रन (Midnight's Children)</b> के लिए बुकर जीता।<br>• <b>जे.जी. फैरेल</b> ने 1973 में <b>द सीज ऑफ कृष्णापुर</b> के लिए जीता; <b>अनीता देसाई</b> तीन बार शॉर्टलिस्ट हुईं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000070016","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Books and Authors","question":{"en":"Which book by Vikram Chandra won the Commonwealth Writers’ Prize for Best First Book in 1996? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"विक्रम चंद्रा की किस पुस्तक ने 1996 में सर्वश्रेष्ठ प्रथम पुस्तक के लिए कॉमनवेल्थ राइटर्स पुरस्कार जीता? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Love and Longing in Bombay","hi":"लव एंड लॉन्गिंग इन बॉम्बे"},"2":{"en":"Sacred Games","hi":"सेक्रेड गेम्स"},"3":{"en":"Red Earth and Pouring Rain","hi":"रेड अर्थ एंड पोरिंग रेन"},"4":{"en":"The Gypsy Goddess","hi":"द जिप्सी गॉडेस"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Red Earth and Pouring Rain</b><br>Vikram Chandra's debut novel <b><u>Red Earth and Pouring Rain</u></b> (1995) won the <b>Commonwealth Writers' Prize for Best First Book</b> in 1996.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Love and Longing in Bombay</b> (1997) – Vikram Chandra's short story collection.<br>• <b>Sacred Games</b> (2006) – his crime novel, later adapted into a Netflix series.<br>• <b>The Gypsy Goddess</b> (2014) is by <b>Meena Kandasamy</b>, not Vikram Chandra.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – रेड अर्थ एंड पोरिंग रेन</b><br>विक्रम चंद्रा के पहले उपन्यास <b><u>रेड अर्थ एंड पोरिंग रेन (Red Earth and Pouring Rain)</u></b> (1995) ने 1996 में <b>सर्वश्रेष्ठ प्रथम पुस्तक का कॉमनवेल्थ राइटर्स पुरस्कार</b> जीता।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>लव एंड लॉन्गिंग इन बॉम्बे</b> (1997) – विक्रम चंद्रा का कहानी-संग्रह।<br>• <b>सेक्रेड गेम्स</b> (2006) – उनका अपराध उपन्यास, जिस पर नेटफ्लिक्स सीरीज़ बनी।<br>• <b>द जिप्सी गॉडेस</b> (2014) <b>मीना कंदासामी</b> की रचना है, विक्रम चंद्रा की नहीं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000070017","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"The Twenty-Point Programme (TPP), introduced during the ________ Five-Year Plan. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"बीस सूत्री कार्यक्रम (TPP) ________ पंचवर्षीय योजना के दौरान शुरू किया गया। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"6<sup>th</sup>","hi":"छठी"},"2":{"en":"7<sup>th</sup>","hi":"सातवीं"},"3":{"en":"8<sup>th</sup>","hi":"आठवीं"},"4":{"en":"5<sup>th</sup>","hi":"पाँचवीं"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – 5<sup>th</sup></b><br>The <b>Twenty-Point Programme</b> was launched by PM <b>Indira Gandhi in 1975</b>, during the <b><u>Fifth Five-Year Plan</u></b> (1974–79), to fight poverty and improve living standards.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The programme was restructured in <b>1982, 1986 and 2006</b> (TPP-2006).<br>• Fifth Plan slogan: <b>\"Garibi Hatao\"</b>; its draft was prepared by <b>D.P. Dhar</b>.<br>• It is monitored by the <b>Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation (MoSPI)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – पाँचवीं</b><br><b>बीस सूत्री कार्यक्रम</b> प्रधानमंत्री <b>इंदिरा गांधी ने 1975</b> में <b><u>पाँचवीं पंचवर्षीय योजना</u></b> (1974–79) के दौरान गरीबी उन्मूलन और जीवन स्तर सुधारने के लिए शुरू किया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इस कार्यक्रम का पुनर्गठन <b>1982, 1986 और 2006</b> (TPP-2006) में किया गया।<br>• पाँचवीं योजना का नारा: <b>\"गरीबी हटाओ\"</b>; इसका प्रारूप <b>डी.पी. धर</b> ने तैयार किया।<br>• इसकी निगरानी <b>सांख्यिकी और कार्यक्रम कार्यान्वयन मंत्रालय (MoSPI)</b> करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000070018","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"The Teej Festival marks the arrival of which season in India? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"तीज त्योहार भारत में किस ऋतु के आगमन का प्रतीक है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Summer","hi":"ग्रीष्म"},"2":{"en":"Spring","hi":"वसंत"},"3":{"en":"Monsoon","hi":"मानसून"},"4":{"en":"Winter","hi":"शीत"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Monsoon</b><br><b>Teej</b> is celebrated in the month of <b>Shravan</b> to welcome the <b><u>monsoon</u></b>, mainly by women, and is dedicated to Goddess Parvati.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Popular in <b>Rajasthan, Haryana, Uttar Pradesh, Bihar</b> and Nepal; swings and green attire are common.<br>• Types: <b>Hariyali Teej, Kajari Teej and Hartalika Teej</b>.<br>• <b>Basant Panchami</b> marks spring; <b>Lohri</b> marks the end of peak winter.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – मानसून</b><br><b>तीज</b> <b>श्रावण</b> मास में <b><u>मानसून</u></b> के स्वागत में मुख्यतः महिलाओं द्वारा मनाई जाती है और देवी पार्वती को समर्पित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>राजस्थान, हरियाणा, उत्तर प्रदेश, बिहार</b> और नेपाल में लोकप्रिय; झूले और हरे वस्त्र प्रचलित हैं।<br>• प्रकार: <b>हरियाली तीज, कजरी तीज और हरतालिका तीज</b>।<br>• <b>बसंत पंचमी</b> वसंत का और <b>लोहड़ी</b> कड़ाके की सर्दी के अंत का प्रतीक है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000070019","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"The introduction of English as the medium of instruction in Indian schools was largely a result of the recommendations made by: [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारतीय विद्यालयों में शिक्षा के माध्यम के रूप में अंग्रेज़ी की शुरुआत मुख्य रूप से किसकी सिफारिशों का परिणाम थी? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The Hunter Commission","hi":"हंटर आयोग"},"2":{"en":"The Wood's Despatch","hi":"वुड का डिस्पैच"},"3":{"en":"The Sadler Commission","hi":"सैडलर आयोग"},"4":{"en":"The Sargent Scheme","hi":"सार्जेंट योजना"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – The Wood's Despatch</b><br><b>Wood's Despatch (1854)</b>, the \"Magna Carta of English Education in India\", recommended <b><u>English as the medium of higher education</u></b> and vernaculars at the school level, and set up a graded system of schools to universities.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Led to universities at <b>Calcutta, Bombay and Madras in 1857</b>.<br>• <b>Hunter Commission (1882)</b> – primary and secondary education; <b>Sadler Commission (1917–19)</b> – Calcutta University.<br>• <b>Sargent Plan (1944)</b> – national education scheme for post-war India.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – वुड का डिस्पैच</b><br><b>वुड का डिस्पैच (1854)</b>, जिसे \"भारत में अंग्रेज़ी शिक्षा का मैग्नाकार्टा\" कहा जाता है, ने <b><u>उच्च शिक्षा के माध्यम के रूप में अंग्रेज़ी</u></b> और विद्यालय स्तर पर देशी भाषाओं की सिफारिश की तथा विद्यालय से विश्वविद्यालय तक श्रेणीबद्ध व्यवस्था बनाई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसके परिणामस्वरूप <b>1857 में कलकत्ता, बॉम्बे और मद्रास</b> विश्वविद्यालय स्थापित हुए।<br>• <b>हंटर आयोग (1882)</b> – प्राथमिक व माध्यमिक शिक्षा; <b>सैडलर आयोग (1917–19)</b> – कलकत्ता विश्वविद्यालय।<br>• <b>सार्जेंट योजना (1944)</b> – युद्धोत्तर भारत के लिए राष्ट्रीय शिक्षा योजना।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000070020","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"Which Indian cricket stadium hosted the 2023 ICC World Cup final? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किस भारतीय क्रिकेट स्टेडियम ने 2023 ICC विश्व कप फाइनल की मेज़बानी की? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Wankhede Stadium","hi":"वानखेड़े स्टेडियम"},"2":{"en":"M. Chinnaswamy Stadium","hi":"एम. चिन्नास्वामी स्टेडियम"},"3":{"en":"Narendra Modi Stadium","hi":"नरेंद्र मोदी स्टेडियम"},"4":{"en":"Eden Gardens","hi":"ईडन गार्डन्स"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Narendra Modi Stadium</b><br>The 2023 ICC Men's Cricket World Cup final was played on <b>19 November 2023</b> at the <b><u>Narendra Modi Stadium, Ahmedabad</u></b>, where <b>Australia</b> beat India.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Narendra Modi Stadium (formerly <b>Motera</b>) is the <b>world's largest cricket stadium</b> (capacity about 1,32,000).<br>• Australia won its <b>sixth</b> ODI World Cup title; <b>Travis Head</b> was Player of the Match.<br>• <b>Wankhede (Mumbai)</b> hosted the 2011 World Cup final won by India.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – नरेंद्र मोदी स्टेडियम</b><br>2023 ICC पुरुष क्रिकेट विश्व कप फाइनल <b>19 नवंबर 2023</b> को <b><u>नरेंद्र मोदी स्टेडियम, अहमदाबाद</u></b> में खेला गया, जहाँ <b>ऑस्ट्रेलिया</b> ने भारत को हराया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• नरेंद्र मोदी स्टेडियम (पूर्व नाम <b>मोटेरा</b>) <b>विश्व का सबसे बड़ा क्रिकेट स्टेडियम</b> है (क्षमता लगभग 1,32,000)।<br>• ऑस्ट्रेलिया ने अपना <b>छठा</b> वनडे विश्व कप जीता; <b>ट्रैविस हेड</b> प्लेयर ऑफ द मैच रहे।<br>• <b>वानखेड़े (मुंबई)</b> में 2011 विश्व कप फाइनल हुआ था, जिसे भारत ने जीता।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000070021","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"Which of the following women freedom fighters was known as the ‘Agni of India’? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से किस महिला स्वतंत्रता सेनानी को ‘भारत की अग्नि’ के नाम से जाना जाता था? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Durgawati Devi","hi":"दुर्गावती देवी"},"2":{"en":"Kamaladevi Chattopadhyay","hi":"कमलादेवी चट्टोपाध्याय"},"3":{"en":"Captain Lakshmi Sehgal","hi":"कैप्टन लक्ष्मी सहगल"},"4":{"en":"Usha Mehta","hi":"उषा मेहता"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Durgawati Devi</b><br><b>Durgawati Devi</b>, popularly called <b>\"Durga Bhabhi\"</b>, was a revolutionary associated with Bhagat Singh's <b>HSRA</b> and is remembered as the <b><u>‘Agni of India’</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• She helped <b>Bhagat Singh</b> escape from Lahore in disguise after the Saunders killing (1928).<br>• <b>Captain Lakshmi Sehgal</b> – commander of the <b>Rani of Jhansi Regiment</b> of the INA.<br>• <b>Usha Mehta</b> – ran the secret <b>Congress Radio</b> during the Quit India Movement (1942).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – दुर्गावती देवी</b><br><b>दुर्गावती देवी</b>, जिन्हें <b>\"दुर्गा भाभी\"</b> कहा जाता था, भगत सिंह के <b>HSRA</b> से जुड़ी क्रांतिकारी थीं और उन्हें <b><u>‘भारत की अग्नि’</u></b> के रूप में याद किया जाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सॉन्डर्स हत्याकांड (1928) के बाद उन्होंने <b>भगत सिंह</b> को भेष बदलकर लाहौर से निकलने में मदद की।<br>• <b>कैप्टन लक्ष्मी सहगल</b> – INA की <b>रानी झाँसी रेजिमेंट</b> की कमांडर।<br>• <b>उषा मेहता</b> – भारत छोड़ो आंदोलन (1942) के दौरान गुप्त <b>कांग्रेस रेडियो</b> चलाया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000070022","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Agriculture","question":{"en":"Regarding pulse production in India, consider the following statements.<br>1. Black gram can be cultivated as both kharif and Rabi crops.<br>2. Green gram alone accounts for nearly half of pulse production.<br>3. In the last three decades, while the production of Kharif pulses has increased, the production of Rabi pulses has decreased.<br>Which of the statements given above is/are CORRECT? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत में दलहन उत्पादन के संबंध में निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार कीजिए।<br>1. उड़द को खरीफ और रबी दोनों फसलों के रूप में उगाया जा सकता है।<br>2. अकेले मूँग दलहन उत्पादन का लगभग आधा भाग है।<br>3. पिछले तीन दशकों में खरीफ दलहन का उत्पादन बढ़ा है, जबकि रबी दलहन का उत्पादन घटा है।<br>ऊपर दिए गए कथनों में से कौन-सा/से सही है/हैं? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 only","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"2 and 3 only","hi":"केवल 2 और 3"},"3":{"en":"2 only","hi":"केवल 2"},"4":{"en":"1 and 2 only","hi":"केवल 1 और 2"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – 1 only</b><br>Statement 1 is correct: <b>black gram (urad)</b> is grown in both seasons. Statement 2 is wrong: <b>gram (chana)</b>, not green gram, gives nearly half of pulse output. Statement 3 is wrong: <b>rabi pulse</b> output has risen sharply. Hence <b><u>1 only</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India is the <b>largest producer, consumer and importer</b> of pulses in the world.<br>• Leading pulse-producing states: <b>Madhya Pradesh, Maharashtra, Rajasthan</b>.<br>• 2016 was observed as the <b>International Year of Pulses</b>; 10 February is <b>World Pulses Day</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – केवल 1</b><br>कथन 1 सही है: <b>उड़द (Black gram)</b> दोनों मौसमों में उगाई जाती है। कथन 2 गलत है: दलहन उत्पादन का लगभग आधा भाग <b>चना (Gram)</b> देता है, मूँग नहीं। कथन 3 गलत है: <b>रबी दलहन</b> का उत्पादन तेज़ी से बढ़ा है। अतः <b><u>केवल 1</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत विश्व में दलहन का <b>सबसे बड़ा उत्पादक, उपभोक्ता और आयातक</b> है।<br>• प्रमुख दलहन उत्पादक राज्य: <b>मध्य प्रदेश, महाराष्ट्र, राजस्थान</b>।<br>• 2016 को <b>अंतर्राष्ट्रीय दलहन वर्ष</b> मनाया गया; 10 फरवरी <b>विश्व दलहन दिवस</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000070023","section":"GK","topic":"Biology: Hormones and Plant Movement","question":{"en":"What is the major health risk associated with long-term use of anabolic steroids by athletes? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"खिलाड़ियों द्वारा एनाबॉलिक स्टेरॉयड के दीर्घकालिक उपयोग से जुड़ा प्रमुख स्वास्थ्य जोखिम क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Increased bone thickness and strength","hi":"हड्डियों की मोटाई और मज़बूती में वृद्धि"},"2":{"en":"Severe dehydration and fluid loss","hi":"गंभीर निर्जलीकरण और द्रव की हानि"},"3":{"en":"Hormonal imbalance and organ damage","hi":"हार्मोनल असंतुलन और अंगों को क्षति"},"4":{"en":"Better immunity and faster recovery","hi":"बेहतर प्रतिरक्षा और तेज़ रिकवरी"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Hormonal imbalance and organ damage</b><br>Anabolic steroids are synthetic forms of <b>testosterone</b>. Long-term use causes <b><u>hormonal imbalance</u></b> and damages the <b>liver, heart and kidneys</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Side effects include infertility, gynaecomastia in males, masculinisation in females, high BP and liver tumours.<br>• They are banned by the <b>World Anti-Doping Agency (WADA)</b>, HQ <b>Montreal</b>.<br>• India's anti-doping body is <b>NADA</b>, set up in <b>2005</b>; the National Anti-Doping Act was passed in <b>2022</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – हार्मोनल असंतुलन और अंगों को क्षति</b><br>एनाबॉलिक स्टेरॉयड <b>टेस्टोस्टेरोन (Testosterone)</b> के कृत्रिम रूप हैं। लंबे समय तक उपयोग से <b><u>हार्मोनल असंतुलन</u></b> होता है और <b>यकृत, हृदय तथा गुर्दों</b> को क्षति पहुँचती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• दुष्प्रभावों में बांझपन, पुरुषों में गाइनेकोमास्टिया, महिलाओं में पुरुष लक्षण, उच्च रक्तचाप और यकृत ट्यूमर शामिल हैं।<br>• <b>विश्व डोपिंग रोधी एजेंसी (WADA)</b> द्वारा प्रतिबंधित, मुख्यालय <b>मॉन्ट्रियल</b>।<br>• भारत की डोपिंग रोधी संस्था <b>NADA</b> है, स्थापना <b>2005</b>; राष्ट्रीय डोपिंग रोधी अधिनियम <b>2022</b> में पारित हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000070024","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Salient Features of the Constitution","question":{"en":"The doctrine of <b>Basic Structure</b> of the Constitution was propounded in which case and relates to which Article? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"संविधान के <b>मूल ढाँचे</b> का सिद्धांत किस मामले में प्रतिपादित किया गया था और यह किस अनुच्छेद से संबंधित है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Kesavananda Bharati Case; Article 368","hi":"केशवानंद भारती मामला; अनुच्छेद 368"},"2":{"en":"Golaknath Case; Article 21","hi":"गोलकनाथ मामला; अनुच्छेद 21"},"3":{"en":"Maneka Gandhi Case; Article 14","hi":"मेनका गांधी मामला; अनुच्छेद 14"},"4":{"en":"Minerva Mills Case; Article 356","hi":"मिनर्वा मिल्स मामला; अनुच्छेद 356"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Kesavananda Bharati Case; Article 368</b><br>In <b>Kesavananda Bharati v. State of Kerala (1973)</b>, a 13-judge bench held that Parliament can amend the Constitution under <b><u>Article 368</u></b> but cannot alter its <b>basic structure</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Decided by a <b>7:6 majority</b> – the largest bench in Supreme Court history.<br>• <b>Golaknath (1967)</b> – Parliament cannot amend Fundamental Rights; <b>Maneka Gandhi (1978)</b> – widened Article 21.<br>• <b>Minerva Mills (1980)</b> – judicial review and balance between FRs and DPSPs are part of the basic structure.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – केशवानंद भारती मामला; अनुच्छेद 368</b><br><b>केशवानंद भारती बनाम केरल राज्य (1973)</b> में 13 न्यायाधीशों की पीठ ने कहा कि संसद <b><u>अनुच्छेद 368</u></b> के तहत संविधान में संशोधन कर सकती है, परंतु उसके <b>मूल ढाँचे (Basic structure)</b> को नहीं बदल सकती।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>7:6 बहुमत</b> से निर्णय – सर्वोच्च न्यायालय के इतिहास की सबसे बड़ी पीठ।<br>• <b>गोलकनाथ (1967)</b> – संसद मौलिक अधिकारों में संशोधन नहीं कर सकती; <b>मेनका गांधी (1978)</b> – अनुच्छेद 21 का दायरा बढ़ाया।<br>• <b>मिनर्वा मिल्स (1980)</b> – न्यायिक समीक्षा तथा मौलिक अधिकारों और नीति निदेशक तत्वों (DPSP) के बीच संतुलन मूल ढाँचे का भाग है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000070025","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Centre-State Relations","question":{"en":"<b>Arrange the following developments in federal structure chronologically:</b><br>1. Formation of Inter-State Council<br>2. 73<sup>rd</sup> Constitutional Amendment<br>3. GST Council formation [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"<b>संघीय ढाँचे में निम्नलिखित घटनाक्रमों को कालक्रमानुसार व्यवस्थित कीजिए:</b><br>1. अंतर-राज्य परिषद का गठन<br>2. 73वाँ संविधान संशोधन<br>3. GST परिषद का गठन [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1-2-3"},"2":{"en":"3-2-1"},"3":{"en":"2-3-1"},"4":{"en":"1-3-2"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – 1-2-3</b><br><b>Inter-State Council</b> was set up in <b>1990</b> (Art. 263), the <b>73<sup>rd</sup> Amendment</b> was passed in <b>1992</b>, and the <b>GST Council</b> was formed in <b>2016</b>. Order: <b><u>1-2-3</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Inter-State Council was set up on the recommendation of the <b>Sarkaria Commission</b>; chaired by the <b>Prime Minister</b>.<br>• 73<sup>rd</sup> Amendment (in force 1993) added <b>Part IX</b> and the <b>11<sup>th</sup> Schedule</b> (Panchayats, 29 subjects).<br>• GST Council – <b>Article 279A</b>, added by the <b>101<sup>st</sup> Amendment (2016)</b>; chaired by the Union Finance Minister.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – 1-2-3</b><br><b>अंतर-राज्य परिषद</b> <b>1990</b> (अनु. 263) में गठित हुई, <b>73वाँ संशोधन</b> <b>1992</b> में पारित हुआ और <b>GST परिषद</b> <b>2016</b> में बनी। क्रम: <b><u>1-2-3</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• अंतर-राज्य परिषद <b>सरकारिया आयोग (Sarkaria Commission)</b> की सिफारिश पर बनी; अध्यक्ष <b>प्रधानमंत्री</b>।<br>• 73वाँ संशोधन (1993 में लागू) ने <b>भाग IX</b> और <b>11वीं अनुसूची</b> (पंचायतें, 29 विषय) जोड़ी।<br>• GST परिषद – <b>अनुच्छेद 279A</b>, <b>101वें संशोधन (2016)</b> द्वारा जोड़ा गया; अध्यक्ष केंद्रीय वित्त मंत्री।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000070026","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Earth's Interior and Plate Tectonics & Latitude and Longitude","question":{"en":"What does the term \"astheno\" mean in the context of the Earth's mantle? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"पृथ्वी के मेंटल के संदर्भ में \"एस्थेनो\" शब्द का क्या अर्थ है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Strong","hi":"मज़बूत"},"2":{"en":"Weak","hi":"कमज़ोर"},"3":{"en":"Solid","hi":"ठोस"},"4":{"en":"Molten","hi":"पिघला हुआ"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Weak</b><br>The word <b>asthenosphere</b> comes from the Greek <b>\"asthenēs\"</b> meaning <b><u>weak</u></b>. It is the weak, ductile, partly molten zone of the upper mantle below the lithosphere.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Asthenosphere extends roughly up to <b>400 km</b> depth and is the main source of <b>magma</b>.<br>• Lithospheric plates move over the asthenosphere – basis of <b>plate tectonics</b>.<br>• The mantle–crust boundary is the <b>Mohorovičić (Moho) discontinuity</b>; core–mantle boundary is the <b>Gutenberg discontinuity</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – कमज़ोर</b><br><b>एस्थेनोस्फीयर (Asthenosphere)</b> शब्द यूनानी <b>\"asthenēs\"</b> से बना है, जिसका अर्थ <b><u>कमज़ोर</u></b> है। यह स्थलमंडल के नीचे ऊपरी मेंटल का कमज़ोर, लचीला, आंशिक रूप से पिघला क्षेत्र है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• एस्थेनोस्फीयर लगभग <b>400 km</b> गहराई तक फैला है और <b>मैग्मा</b> का मुख्य स्रोत है।<br>• स्थलमंडलीय प्लेटें एस्थेनोस्फीयर पर गति करती हैं – <b>प्लेट विवर्तनिकी (Plate tectonics)</b> का आधार।<br>• मेंटल-भूपर्पटी की सीमा <b>मोहोरोविसिक (मोहो) असांतत्य</b>; क्रोड-मेंटल सीमा <b>गुटेनबर्ग असांतत्य</b> है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000070027","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Atmosphere","question":{"en":"Consider the following statements about the stratosphere:<br>1. Temperature increases in the lower part of the stratosphere due to the presence of methane gas.<br>2. The ozone layer absorbs solar radiation, leading to a rise in temperature with altitude in this layer.<br>Which of the statements above is/are <b>correct</b>? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"समताप मंडल के बारे में निम्नलिखित कथनों पर विचार कीजिए:<br>1. मीथेन गैस की उपस्थिति के कारण समताप मंडल के निचले भाग में तापमान बढ़ता है।<br>2. ओज़ोन परत सौर विकिरण को अवशोषित करती है, जिससे इस परत में ऊँचाई के साथ तापमान बढ़ता है।<br>ऊपर दिए गए कथनों में से कौन-सा/से <b>सही</b> है/हैं? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only 1","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"Only 2","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2 are correct","hi":"1 और 2 दोनों सही हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither 1 nor 2 is correct","hi":"न तो 1 और न ही 2 सही है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Only 2</b><br>The rise of temperature in the stratosphere is due to <b>ozone absorbing ultraviolet radiation</b>, not methane. So statement 1 is wrong and statement 2 is correct: <b><u>Only 2</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Stratosphere extends from the tropopause to about <b>50 km</b>; ozone layer lies mainly at <b>15–35 km</b>.<br>• It is free of weather disturbances, so ideal for <b>jet aircraft</b>.<br>• Ozone is measured in <b>Dobson Units</b>; the <b>Montreal Protocol (1987)</b> protects the ozone layer.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – केवल 2</b><br>समताप मंडल में तापमान वृद्धि <b>ओज़ोन द्वारा पराबैंगनी (UV) विकिरण के अवशोषण</b> से होती है, मीथेन से नहीं। अतः कथन 1 गलत और कथन 2 सही है: <b><u>केवल 2</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• समताप मंडल क्षोभसीमा से लगभग <b>50 km</b> तक फैला है; ओज़ोन परत मुख्यतः <b>15–35 km</b> पर है।<br>• यह मौसमी विक्षोभों से मुक्त है, इसलिए <b>जेट विमानों</b> के लिए आदर्श है।<br>• ओज़ोन को <b>डॉबसन इकाई (Dobson Unit)</b> में मापा जाता है; <b>मॉन्ट्रियल प्रोटोकॉल (1987)</b> ओज़ोन परत की रक्षा करता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000070028","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Which aspect of agriculture witnessed a decline after the economic reforms of 1991? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"1991 के आर्थिक सुधारों के बाद कृषि के किस पहलू में गिरावट देखी गई? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Public investment in agricultural infrastructure","hi":"कृषि अवसंरचना में सार्वजनिक निवेश"},"2":{"en":"Private investment in agricultural development","hi":"कृषि विकास में निजी निवेश"},"3":{"en":"Agricultural exports in international markets","hi":"अंतर्राष्ट्रीय बाज़ारों में कृषि निर्यात"},"4":{"en":"Production of commercial agricultural crops","hi":"वाणिज्यिक कृषि फसलों का उत्पादन"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Public investment in agricultural infrastructure</b><br>After 1991, fiscal tightening reduced government spending, so <b><u>public investment in agricultural infrastructure</u></b> (irrigation, power, rural roads, research) declined, slowing agricultural growth.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The 1991 reforms are known as the <b>LPG reforms</b> – Liberalisation, Privatisation, Globalisation.<br>• Introduced by PM <b>P.V. Narasimha Rao</b> and Finance Minister <b>Dr. Manmohan Singh</b>.<br>• Agricultural exports and cultivation of commercial crops actually <b>rose</b> after trade liberalisation.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – कृषि अवसंरचना में सार्वजनिक निवेश</b><br>1991 के बाद राजकोषीय सख्ती से सरकारी व्यय घटा, इसलिए <b><u>कृषि अवसंरचना में सार्वजनिक निवेश</u></b> (सिंचाई, बिजली, ग्रामीण सड़कें, अनुसंधान) में गिरावट आई और कृषि वृद्धि धीमी हुई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 1991 के सुधारों को <b>LPG सुधार</b> कहते हैं – उदारीकरण (Liberalisation), निजीकरण (Privatisation), वैश्वीकरण (Globalisation)।<br>• प्रधानमंत्री <b>पी.वी. नरसिम्हा राव</b> और वित्त मंत्री <b>डॉ. मनमोहन सिंह</b> द्वारा लागू।<br>• व्यापार उदारीकरण के बाद कृषि निर्यात और वाणिज्यिक फसलों की खेती वास्तव में <b>बढ़ी</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000070029","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"One mole of an ideal gas undergoes a reversible isothermal expansion from 10 L(liter) to 20 L (liter) at a constant temperature of 300 K (kelvin). What is the work done by the gas, approximately? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक मोल आदर्श गैस 300 K (केल्विन) के स्थिर तापमान पर 10 L (लीटर) से 20 L (लीटर) तक उत्क्रमणीय समतापीय प्रसार करती है। गैस द्वारा किया गया कार्य लगभग कितना है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"0 (joule)","hi":"0 (जूल)"},"2":{"en":"700 (joule)","hi":"700 (जूल)"},"3":{"en":"3500 (joule)","hi":"3500 (जूल)"},"4":{"en":"1700 (joule)","hi":"1700 (जूल)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – 1700 (joule)</b><br>For a reversible isothermal process, \\(W = nRT \\ln\\frac{V_2}{V_1}\\)<br>\\(W = 1 \\times 8.314 \\times 300 \\times \\ln 2 = 2494.2 \\times 0.693 \\approx 1729\\) J ≈ <b><u>1700 J</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• In an isothermal process of an ideal gas, internal energy does not change (\\(\\Delta U = 0\\)), so heat absorbed = work done.<br>• Universal gas constant <b>R = 8.314 J mol<sup>−1</sup> K<sup>−1</sup></b>.<br>• Work is zero in an <b>isochoric</b> process (constant volume); in an <b>adiabatic</b> process no heat is exchanged (Q = 0).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – 1700 (जूल)</b><br>उत्क्रमणीय समतापीय प्रक्रम के लिए \\(W = nRT \\ln\\frac{V_2}{V_1}\\)<br>\\(W = 1 \\times 8.314 \\times 300 \\times \\ln 2 = 2494.2 \\times 0.693 \\approx 1729\\) J ≈ <b><u>1700 J</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• आदर्श गैस के समतापीय प्रक्रम में आंतरिक ऊर्जा नहीं बदलती (\\(\\Delta U = 0\\)), अतः अवशोषित ऊष्मा = किया गया कार्य।<br>• सार्वत्रिक गैस नियतांक <b>R = 8.314 J mol<sup>−1</sup> K<sup>−1</sup></b>।<br>• <b>समआयतनिक (Isochoric)</b> प्रक्रम में कार्य शून्य होता है; <b>रुद्धोष्म (Adiabatic)</b> प्रक्रम में ऊष्मा का आदान-प्रदान नहीं होता (Q = 0)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000070030","section":"GK","topic":"Biology: Diseases","question":{"en":"Which process is most directly responsible for the majority of cancer-related deaths? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कैंसर से संबंधित अधिकांश मौतों के लिए सबसे प्रत्यक्ष रूप से कौन-सी प्रक्रिया उत्तरदायी है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Increased local proliferation of tumor cells","hi":"ट्यूमर कोशिकाओं का स्थानीय प्रसार बढ़ना"},"2":{"en":"Loss of cell cycle checkpoints in dividing cells","hi":"विभाजित कोशिकाओं में कोशिका चक्र जाँच-बिंदुओं का नष्ट होना"},"3":{"en":"Formation of metastases in distant organs","hi":"दूरस्थ अंगों में मेटास्टेसिस का बनना"},"4":{"en":"Formation of benign tumor masses in primary tissue","hi":"प्राथमिक ऊतक में सौम्य ट्यूमर का बनना"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Formation of metastases in distant organs</b><br>Around <b>90% of cancer deaths</b> are caused by <b><u>metastasis</u></b> – the spread of cancer cells through blood or lymph to form secondary tumours in distant organs such as lungs, liver, bones and brain.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Benign tumours</b> stay confined to their original site; <b>malignant tumours</b> invade and spread.<br>• Cancer-causing agents are called <b>carcinogens</b> (e.g., UV rays, X-rays, tobacco).<br>• Types: <b>Carcinoma</b> (epithelial tissue), <b>Sarcoma</b> (connective tissue), <b>Leukaemia</b> (blood), <b>Lymphoma</b> (lymph nodes).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – दूरस्थ अंगों में मेटास्टेसिस का बनना</b><br>लगभग <b>90% कैंसर मौतें</b> <b><u>मेटास्टेसिस (Metastasis)</u></b> के कारण होती हैं – कैंसर कोशिकाओं का रक्त या लसीका द्वारा फैलकर फेफड़े, यकृत, हड्डियों और मस्तिष्क जैसे दूरस्थ अंगों में द्वितीयक ट्यूमर बनाना।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>सौम्य ट्यूमर (Benign tumour)</b> अपने मूल स्थान तक सीमित रहते हैं; <b>घातक ट्यूमर (Malignant tumour)</b> आसपास फैलते हैं।<br>• कैंसर उत्पन्न करने वाले कारकों को <b>कैंसरजन (Carcinogens)</b> कहते हैं (जैसे UV किरणें, X-किरणें, तंबाकू)।<br>• प्रकार: <b>कार्सिनोमा</b> (उपकला ऊतक), <b>सार्कोमा</b> (संयोजी ऊतक), <b>ल्यूकेमिया</b> (रक्त), <b>लिम्फोमा</b> (लसीका ग्रंथियाँ)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000070031","section":"MATH","topic":"Simple Interest (SI)","question":{"en":"A sum of money amounts to Rs. 825 in 3 years and to Rs. 950 in 4 years at some rate of simple interest. The sum is: [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कोई धनराशि किसी साधारण ब्याज दर पर 3 वर्षों में Rs. 825 और 4 वर्षों में Rs. 950 हो जाती है। वह धनराशि है: [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"400/-"},"2":{"en":"410/-"},"3":{"en":"450/-"},"4":{"en":"550/-"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Interest for the 4th year alone \\(= 950 - 825 = 125\\)<br>Simple interest is the same every year, so SI for 3 years \\(= 3 \\times 125 = 375\\)<br>Principal \\(= 825 - 375 = \\boxed{450}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 450/-.</b>","hi":"केवल चौथे वर्ष का ब्याज \\(= 950 - 825 = 125\\)<br>साधारण ब्याज हर वर्ष समान होता है, अतः 3 वर्षों का ब्याज \\(= 3 \\times 125 = 375\\)<br>मूलधन \\(= 825 - 375 = \\boxed{450}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 450/- है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000070032","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A toy is in the form of a hemisphere surmounted by a cone. The radius of the hemisphere is 3 cm and the cone's height is 4 cm. Find the total volume of the toy (use π ≈ 3.14). [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक खिलौना एक अर्धगोले के ऊपर शंकु के आकार का है। अर्धगोले की त्रिज्या 3 cm और शंकु की ऊँचाई 4 cm है। खिलौने का कुल आयतन ज्ञात कीजिए (π ≈ 3.14 लीजिए)। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"113.04 cm³"},"2":{"en":"94.2 cm³"},"3":{"en":"188.4 cm³"},"4":{"en":"62.8 cm³"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Volume of the cone \\(= \\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 3.14 \\times 9 \\times 4 = 37.68\\) cm³<br>Volume of the hemisphere \\(= \\frac{2}{3}\\pi r^3 = \\frac{2}{3} \\times 3.14 \\times 27 = 56.52\\) cm³<br>Total \\(= 37.68 + 56.52 = \\boxed{94.2\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 94.2 cm³.</b>","hi":"शंकु का आयतन \\(= \\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 3.14 \\times 9 \\times 4 = 37.68\\) cm³<br>अर्धगोले का आयतन \\(= \\frac{2}{3}\\pi r^3 = \\frac{2}{3} \\times 3.14 \\times 27 = 56.52\\) cm³<br>कुल \\(= 37.68 + 56.52 = \\boxed{94.2\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 94.2 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000070033","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"Solve: \\((x + 2)^2 - (x - 2)^2\\) [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"हल कीजिए: \\((x + 2)^2 - (x - 2)^2\\) [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8x"},"2":{"en":"2x + 4"},"3":{"en":"10x"},"4":{"en":"x²"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\((x+2)^2 = x^2 + 4x + 4\\) and \\((x-2)^2 = x^2 - 4x + 4\\)<br>Difference \\(= (x^2 + 4x + 4) - (x^2 - 4x + 4) = 8x\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{8x}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 8x.</b>","hi":"\\((x+2)^2 = x^2 + 4x + 4\\) और \\((x-2)^2 = x^2 - 4x + 4\\)<br>अंतर \\(= (x^2 + 4x + 4) - (x^2 - 4x + 4) = 8x\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{8x}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 8x है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000070034","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"If the diameter of a circle is 28 cm, then its area is: [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि किसी वृत्त का व्यास 28 cm है, तो उसका क्षेत्रफल है: [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"154 cm²"},"2":{"en":"616 cm²"},"3":{"en":"308 cm²"},"4":{"en":"484 cm²"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Radius \\(r = \\frac{28}{2} = 14\\) cm<br>Area \\(= \\pi r^2 = \\frac{22}{7} \\times 196\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{616\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 616 cm².</b>","hi":"त्रिज्या \\(r = \\frac{28}{2} = 14\\) cm<br>क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\pi r^2 = \\frac{22}{7} \\times 196\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{616\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 616 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000070035","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If tan A + cot A = 2 and A is an acute angle, find the value of tan⁴A + cot⁴A. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि tan A + cot A = 2 और A न्यून कोण है, तो tan⁴A + cot⁴A का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"20"},"3":{"en":"22"},"4":{"en":"24"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\tan A + \\cot A = 2 \\Rightarrow \\tan A = 1\\) (AM-GM equality), so \\(A = 45°\\)<br>Then \\(\\cot A = 1\\) as well<br>\\(\\tan^4 A + \\cot^4 A = 1 + 1 = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2.</b>","hi":"\\(\\tan A + \\cot A = 2 \\Rightarrow \\tan A = 1\\) (AM-GM समता), अतः \\(A = 45°\\)<br>तब \\(\\cot A = 1\\) भी है<br>\\(\\tan^4 A + \\cot^4 A = 1 + 1 = \\boxed{2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 2 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000070036","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A cone has a height of 8 cm and a slant height of 10 cm. What is the volume of the cone? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक शंकु की ऊँचाई 8 cm और तिर्यक ऊँचाई 10 cm है। शंकु का आयतन क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"301.71 cm³"},"2":{"en":"304 cm³"},"3":{"en":"305.75 cm³"},"4":{"en":"308.76 cm³"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Radius \\(r = \\sqrt{l^2 - h^2} = \\sqrt{100 - 64} = 6\\) cm<br>Volume \\(= \\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 36 \\times 8\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{6336}{21} = \\boxed{301.71\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 301.71 cm³.</b>","hi":"त्रिज्या \\(r = \\sqrt{l^2 - h^2} = \\sqrt{100 - 64} = 6\\) cm<br>आयतन \\(= \\frac{1}{3}\\pi r^2 h = \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 36 \\times 8\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{6336}{21} = \\boxed{301.71\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 301.71 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000070037","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"A pyramid has a rectangular base with dimensions 6 cm by 8 cm. If the height of the pyramid is 1.5 times the longer side of the base, calculate the volume of the pyramid. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक पिरामिड का आधार आयताकार है जिसकी विमाएँ 6 cm × 8 cm हैं। यदि पिरामिड की ऊँचाई आधार की बड़ी भुजा की 1.5 गुनी है, तो पिरामिड का आयतन ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"292 cm³"},"2":{"en":"262 cm³"},"3":{"en":"252 cm³"},"4":{"en":"192 cm³"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Base area \\(= 6 \\times 8 = 48\\) cm²; height \\(= 1.5 \\times 8 = 12\\) cm<br>Volume \\(= \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\text{base area} \\times h = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 48 \\times 12\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{192\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 192 cm³.</b>","hi":"आधार क्षेत्रफल \\(= 6 \\times 8 = 48\\) cm²; ऊँचाई \\(= 1.5 \\times 8 = 12\\) cm<br>आयतन \\(= \\frac{1}{3} \\times \\text{आधार क्षेत्रफल} \\times h = \\frac{1}{3} \\times 48 \\times 12\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{192\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 192 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000070038","section":"MATH","topic":"Coordinate Geometry","question":{"en":"What is the distance between points A(2, 3) and B(5, 7)? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"बिंदुओं A(2, 3) और B(5, 7) के बीच की दूरी क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4 units"},"2":{"en":"6 units"},"3":{"en":"7 units"},"4":{"en":"5 units"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(AB = \\sqrt{(5 - 2)^2 + (7 - 3)^2}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{9 + 16} = \\sqrt{25}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{5\\ \\text{units}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 5 units.</b>","hi":"\\(AB = \\sqrt{(5 - 2)^2 + (7 - 3)^2}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{9 + 16} = \\sqrt{25}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{5\\ \\text{units}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 5 units है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000070039","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In △ABC, a line DE is drawn parallel to BC, intersecting AB at D and AC at E. If AD = 3 cm, DB = 2 cm, and DE = 4 cm, what is the length of BC? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"△ABC में BC के समांतर एक रेखा DE खींची गई है, जो AB को D पर और AC को E पर प्रतिच्छेद करती है। यदि AD = 3 cm, DB = 2 cm और DE = 4 cm है, तो BC की लंबाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5 cm"},"2":{"en":"6 cm"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{3}{20}\\) cm"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{20}{3}\\) cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Since \\(DE \\parallel BC\\), \\(\\triangle ADE \\sim \\triangle ABC\\)<br>\\(\\frac{DE}{BC} = \\frac{AD}{AB} = \\frac{3}{3 + 2} = \\frac{3}{5}\\)<br>\\(BC = \\frac{5 \\times 4}{3} = \\boxed{\\frac{20}{3}\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(\\frac{20}{3}\\) cm.</b>","hi":"चूँकि \\(DE \\parallel BC\\), अतः \\(\\triangle ADE \\sim \\triangle ABC\\)<br>\\(\\frac{DE}{BC} = \\frac{AD}{AB} = \\frac{3}{3 + 2} = \\frac{3}{5}\\)<br>\\(BC = \\frac{5 \\times 4}{3} = \\boxed{\\frac{20}{3}\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(\\frac{20}{3}\\) cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000070040","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If x = 1.5 and y = 0.5, find the value of \\(\\frac{x^3 - y^3}{x^2 + xy + y^2} + \\frac{x^3 + y^3}{x^2 - xy + y^2}\\). [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि x = 1.5 और y = 0.5 है, तो \\(\\frac{x^3 - y^3}{x^2 + xy + y^2} + \\frac{x^3 + y^3}{x^2 - xy + y^2}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1"},"2":{"en":"3"},"3":{"en":"2"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{x^3 - y^3}{x^2 + xy + y^2} = x - y = 1.5 - 0.5 = 1\\)<br>\\(\\frac{x^3 + y^3}{x^2 - xy + y^2} = x + y = 1.5 + 0.5 = 2\\)<br>Sum \\(= 1 + 2 = \\boxed{3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 3.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{x^3 - y^3}{x^2 + xy + y^2} = x - y = 1.5 - 0.5 = 1\\)<br>\\(\\frac{x^3 + y^3}{x^2 - xy + y^2} = x + y = 1.5 + 0.5 = 2\\)<br>योग \\(= 1 + 2 = \\boxed{3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 3 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000070041","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A and B can complete a piece of work in 15 days and 20 days respectively. They work on alternate days, starting with A. In how many days will the work be completed? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"A और B एक कार्य को क्रमशः 15 दिनों और 20 दिनों में पूरा कर सकते हैं। वे A से शुरू करते हुए एकांतर दिनों में कार्य करते हैं। कार्य कितने दिनों में पूरा होगा? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"12 days","hi":"12 दिन"},"2":{"en":"15 days","hi":"15 दिन"},"3":{"en":"25 days","hi":"25 दिन"},"4":{"en":"17 days","hi":"17 दिन"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"A's one-day work \\(= \\frac{1}{15}\\), B's \\(= \\frac{1}{20}\\)<br>Work in a 2-day cycle \\(= \\frac{1}{15} + \\frac{1}{20} = \\frac{7}{60}\\)<br>In 8 cycles (16 days) \\(= \\frac{56}{60}\\), remaining \\(\\frac{4}{60} = \\frac{1}{15}\\)<br>Day 17 is A's turn and A finishes \\(\\frac{1}{15}\\) in one day, so the work ends on day 17<br>\\(= \\boxed{17\\ \\text{days}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 17 days.</b>","hi":"A का एक-दिन का कार्य \\(= \\frac{1}{15}\\), B का \\(= \\frac{1}{20}\\)<br>2 दिन के चक्र में कार्य \\(= \\frac{1}{15} + \\frac{1}{20} = \\frac{7}{60}\\)<br>8 चक्रों (16 दिन) में \\(= \\frac{56}{60}\\), शेष \\(\\frac{4}{60} = \\frac{1}{15}\\)<br>17वाँ दिन A की बारी है और A एक दिन में \\(\\frac{1}{15}\\) पूरा कर देता है, अतः कार्य 17वें दिन समाप्त होता है<br>\\(= \\boxed{17\\ \\text{दिन}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 17 दिन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000070042","section":"MATH","topic":"Ratio and Proportion","question":{"en":"An amount of ₹33,630 is distributed among A, B, and C. The ratio of A's share to B's share is 3 : 7, and the ratio of B's share to C's share is 6 : 5. Find the amount of money received by B. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"₹33,630 की राशि A, B और C के बीच वितरित की जाती है। A के हिस्से का B के हिस्से से अनुपात 3 : 7 है और B के हिस्से का C के हिस्से से अनुपात 6 : 5 है। B को मिलने वाली राशि ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹13,290"},"2":{"en":"₹14,868"},"3":{"en":"₹15,327"},"4":{"en":"₹16,409"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A : B = 3 : 7 and B : C = 6 : 5, so taking B = 42<br>A : B : C \\(= 18 : 42 : 35\\), total parts \\(= 95\\)<br>B's share \\(= \\frac{42}{95} \\times 33{,}630 = 42 \\times 354\\)<br>₹\\(= \\boxed{14{,}868}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): ₹14,868.</b>","hi":"A : B = 3 : 7 और B : C = 6 : 5, अतः B = 42 लेने पर<br>A : B : C \\(= 18 : 42 : 35\\), कुल भाग \\(= 95\\)<br>B का हिस्सा \\(= \\frac{42}{95} \\times 33{,}630 = 42 \\times 354\\)<br>₹\\(= \\boxed{14{,}868}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): ₹14,868 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000070043","section":"MATH","topic":"Partnership","question":{"en":"In a company, A is a working partner, and B is a sleeping partner. The investment of A is ₹12,000, and that of B is ₹20,000. The percentage of management charge is 10% of the total gain to be received by A. The total gain is ₹9,600. What is the total gain of A? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक कंपनी में A कार्यशील साझेदार और B निष्क्रिय साझेदार है। A का निवेश ₹12,000 और B का निवेश ₹20,000 है। कुल लाभ के 10% प्रबंधन शुल्क के रूप में A को मिलते हैं। कुल लाभ ₹9,600 है। A का कुल लाभ क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹3,240"},"2":{"en":"₹3,600"},"3":{"en":"₹4,140"},"4":{"en":"₹4,200"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Management charge for A \\(= 10\\%\\) of \\(9{,}600 = 960\\)<br>Remaining profit \\(= 9{,}600 - 960 = 8{,}640\\), shared as \\(12{,}000 : 20{,}000 = 3 : 5\\)<br>A's share of profit \\(= \\frac{3}{8} \\times 8{,}640 = 3{,}240\\)<br>Total gain of A ₹\\(= 960 + 3{,}240 = \\boxed{4{,}200}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ₹4,200.</b>","hi":"A के लिए प्रबंधन शुल्क \\(= 9{,}600\\) का \\(10\\% = 960\\)<br>शेष लाभ \\(= 9{,}600 - 960 = 8{,}640\\), जो \\(12{,}000 : 20{,}000 = 3 : 5\\) में बाँटा जाता है<br>लाभ में A का हिस्सा \\(= \\frac{3}{8} \\times 8{,}640 = 3{,}240\\)<br>A का कुल लाभ ₹\\(= 960 + 3{,}240 = \\boxed{4{,}200}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ₹4,200 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000070044","section":"MATH","topic":"Percentage","question":{"en":"In an election, 10% of the voters did not vote, while 150 votes were found to be invalid. There were only two candidates. The winner secured 55% of the total voters and defeated the opponent by 1100 votes. Find the total number of voters. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक चुनाव में 10% मतदाताओं ने मत नहीं डाला, जबकि 150 मत अवैध पाए गए। केवल दो उम्मीदवार थे। विजेता को कुल मतदाताओं के 55% मत मिले और उसने प्रतिद्वंद्वी को 1100 मतों से हराया। कुल मतदाताओं की संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5360"},"2":{"en":"6230"},"3":{"en":"3440"},"4":{"en":"4750"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Let total voters be \\(N\\); valid votes \\(= 0.9N - 150\\)<br>Winner \\(= 0.55N\\), so the opponent gets \\(0.9N - 150 - 0.55N = 0.35N - 150\\)<br>Difference \\(= (0.55N) - (0.35N - 150) = 0.2N + 150 = 1100\\)<br>\\(0.2N = 950 \\Rightarrow N = \\boxed{4750}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 4750.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए कुल मतदाता \\(N\\) हैं; वैध मत \\(= 0.9N - 150\\)<br>विजेता \\(= 0.55N\\), अतः प्रतिद्वंद्वी को \\(0.9N - 150 - 0.55N = 0.35N - 150\\) मत मिले<br>अंतर \\(= (0.55N) - (0.35N - 150) = 0.2N + 150 = 1100\\)<br>\\(0.2N = 950 \\Rightarrow N = \\boxed{4750}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 4750 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000070045","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"A hexagon is drawn inside a circle with a radius of 21 cm. Determine the area of the hexagon. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"21 cm त्रिज्या वाले एक वृत्त के भीतर एक षट्भुज खींचा गया है। षट्भुज का क्षेत्रफल ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(611.5\\sqrt{9}\\) cm²"},"2":{"en":"\\(661.5\\sqrt{3}\\) cm²"},"3":{"en":"\\(621.5\\sqrt{7}\\) cm²"},"4":{"en":"\\(641.5\\sqrt{3}\\) cm²"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A regular hexagon inscribed in a circle has side \\(= r = 21\\) cm<br>Area \\(= \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}r^2 = \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 441\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1323}{2}\\sqrt{3} = \\boxed{661.5\\sqrt{3}\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(661.5\\sqrt{3}\\) cm².</b>","hi":"वृत्त में अंतर्निहित समषट्भुज की भुजा \\(= r = 21\\) cm<br>क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2}r^2 = \\frac{3\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\times 441\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{1323}{2}\\sqrt{3} = \\boxed{661.5\\sqrt{3}\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(661.5\\sqrt{3}\\) cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000070046","section":"MATH","topic":"Profit and Loss","question":{"en":"A dealer sold two sets of headphones for ₹990 each. On one he gained 10% and on the other he lost 10%. Find the total loss or gain percentage. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक विक्रेता ने हेडफ़ोन के दो सेट ₹990 प्रत्येक पर बेचे। एक पर उसे 10% लाभ और दूसरे पर 10% हानि हुई। कुल लाभ या हानि प्रतिशत ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1% gain","hi":"1% लाभ"},"2":{"en":"1% loss","hi":"1% हानि"},"3":{"en":"2% loss","hi":"2% हानि"},"4":{"en":"No loss or gain","hi":"न लाभ न हानि"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Cost of the first set \\(= \\frac{990}{1.1} = 900\\), cost of the second \\(= \\frac{990}{0.9} = 1100\\)<br>Total cost \\(= 2000\\), total selling price \\(= 1980\\)<br>Loss \\(= 20\\) on \\(2000\\) → \\(\\frac{20}{2000} \\times 100 = \\boxed{1\\%\\ \\text{loss}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 1% loss.</b>","hi":"पहले सेट का क्रय मूल्य \\(= \\frac{990}{1.1} = 900\\), दूसरे का \\(= \\frac{990}{0.9} = 1100\\)<br>कुल क्रय मूल्य \\(= 2000\\), कुल विक्रय मूल्य \\(= 1980\\)<br>हानि \\(= 2000\\) पर \\(20\\) → \\(\\frac{20}{2000} \\times 100 = \\boxed{1\\%\\ \\text{loss}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 1% हानि है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000070047","section":"MATH","topic":"Discount","question":{"en":"A laptop has a marked price of ₹80,000. It is sold after giving successive discounts of 15%, 20% and 10%. Find the selling price. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक लैपटॉप का अंकित मूल्य ₹80,000 है। उसे 15%, 20% और 10% की क्रमिक छूट के बाद बेचा जाता है। विक्रय मूल्य ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"₹54,400"},"2":{"en":"₹47,620"},"3":{"en":"₹50,240"},"4":{"en":"₹48,960"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Selling price \\(= 80{,}000 \\times 0.85 \\times 0.80 \\times 0.90\\)<br>\\(= 80{,}000 \\times 0.612\\)<br>₹\\(= \\boxed{48{,}960}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): ₹48,960.</b>","hi":"विक्रय मूल्य \\(= 80{,}000 \\times 0.85 \\times 0.80 \\times 0.90\\)<br>\\(= 80{,}000 \\times 0.612\\)<br>₹\\(= \\boxed{48{,}960}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): ₹48,960 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000070048","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sin A + \\cos A = \\frac{5}{4}\\), then find the value of \\(\\tan A + \\cot A\\). [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि \\(\\sin A + \\cos A = \\frac{5}{4}\\) है, तो \\(\\tan A + \\cot A\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{32}{9}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{25}{16}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{9}{32}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{16}{25}\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\((\\sin A + \\cos A)^2 = 1 + 2\\sin A\\cos A = \\frac{25}{16}\\)<br>\\(2\\sin A\\cos A = \\frac{9}{16} \\Rightarrow \\sin A\\cos A = \\frac{9}{32}\\)<br>\\(\\tan A + \\cot A = \\frac{\\sin A}{\\cos A} + \\frac{\\cos A}{\\sin A} = \\frac{1}{\\sin A\\cos A} = \\boxed{\\frac{32}{9}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\frac{32}{9}\\).</b>","hi":"\\((\\sin A + \\cos A)^2 = 1 + 2\\sin A\\cos A = \\frac{25}{16}\\)<br>\\(2\\sin A\\cos A = \\frac{9}{16} \\Rightarrow \\sin A\\cos A = \\frac{9}{32}\\)<br>\\(\\tan A + \\cot A = \\frac{\\sin A}{\\cos A} + \\frac{\\cos A}{\\sin A} = \\frac{1}{\\sin A\\cos A} = \\boxed{\\frac{32}{9}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\frac{32}{9}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000070049","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sqrt{2} = 1.414\\), then find the value of \\(\\frac{4 + \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\). [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि \\(\\sqrt{2} = 1.414\\) है, तो \\(\\frac{4 + \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2.124"},"2":{"en":"2.342"},"3":{"en":"3.167"},"4":{"en":"3.828"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{4 + \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}} + 1 = 2\\sqrt{2} + 1\\)<br>\\(= 2(1.414) + 1\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3.828}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 3.828.</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{4 + \\sqrt{2}}{\\sqrt{2}} = \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{2}} + 1 = 2\\sqrt{2} + 1\\)<br>\\(= 2(1.414) + 1\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3.828}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 3.828 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000070050","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If \\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = 3\\sqrt{2}\\), then find the value of \\(\\frac{x}{x^2 - 1}\\). [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि \\(x + \\frac{1}{x} = 3\\sqrt{2}\\) है, तो \\(\\frac{x}{x^2 - 1}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{12}}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{18}}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{19}}\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(\\frac{x}{x^2 - 1} = \\frac{1}{x - \\frac{1}{x}}\\)<br>\\(\\left(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\right)^2 = \\left(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\right)^2 - 4 = 18 - 4 = 14\\)<br>\\(x - \\frac{1}{x} = \\sqrt{14}\\), so the value \\(= \\boxed{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\frac{x}{x^2 - 1} = \\frac{1}{x - \\frac{1}{x}}\\)<br>\\(\\left(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\right)^2 = \\left(x + \\frac{1}{x}\\right)^2 - 4 = 18 - 4 = 14\\)<br>\\(x - \\frac{1}{x} = \\sqrt{14}\\), अतः मान \\(= \\boxed{\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{14}}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000070051","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In a circle of radius 61 cm, two equal parallel chords lie on opposite sides of the centre. The distance between the chords is 22 cm. Find the length of each chord. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"61 cm त्रिज्या वाले एक वृत्त में दो बराबर समांतर जीवाएँ केंद्र के विपरीत ओर स्थित हैं। जीवाओं के बीच की दूरी 22 cm है। प्रत्येक जीवा की लंबाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"30 cm"},"2":{"en":"60 cm"},"3":{"en":"90 cm"},"4":{"en":"120 cm"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"By symmetry each chord is \\(\\frac{22}{2} = 11\\) cm from the centre<br>Half chord \\(= \\sqrt{61^2 - 11^2} = \\sqrt{3721 - 121} = \\sqrt{3600} = 60\\) cm<br>Chord \\(= 2 \\times 60 = \\boxed{120\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 120 cm.</b>","hi":"सममिति से प्रत्येक जीवा केंद्र से \\(\\frac{22}{2} = 11\\) cm दूर है<br>आधी जीवा \\(= \\sqrt{61^2 - 11^2} = \\sqrt{3721 - 121} = \\sqrt{3600} = 60\\) cm<br>जीवा \\(= 2 \\times 60 = \\boxed{120\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 120 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000070052","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"A tangent is drawn from external point Q to a circle having a centre O, touching at T. OT = 6 cm and OQ = 10 cm. What is the area of triangle OTQ? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"बाहरी बिंदु Q से केंद्र O वाले एक वृत्त पर स्पर्श रेखा खींची गई है, जो T पर स्पर्श करती है। OT = 6 cm और OQ = 10 cm है। त्रिभुज OTQ का क्षेत्रफल क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"14 cm²"},"2":{"en":"18 cm²"},"3":{"en":"24 cm²"},"4":{"en":"28 cm²"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(OT \\perp QT\\), so \\(\\triangle OTQ\\) is right-angled at T<br>\\(QT = \\sqrt{10^2 - 6^2} = \\sqrt{64} = 8\\) cm<br>Area \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 \\times 8 = \\boxed{24\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 24 cm².</b>","hi":"\\(OT \\perp QT\\), अतः \\(\\triangle OTQ\\) T पर समकोणीय है<br>\\(QT = \\sqrt{10^2 - 6^2} = \\sqrt{64} = 8\\) cm<br>क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 6 \\times 8 = \\boxed{24\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 24 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000070053","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"Arcs of two circles with radii 15 cm and 20 cm subtend angles of 60° and 45° at their respective centres. What is the ratio of their arc lengths? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"15 cm और 20 cm त्रिज्या वाले दो वृत्तों के चाप अपने-अपने केंद्रों पर 60° और 45° के कोण अंतरित करते हैं। उनके चापों की लंबाइयों का अनुपात क्या है? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1:2"},"2":{"en":"3:1"},"3":{"en":"1:1"},"4":{"en":"2:3"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Arc lengths: \\(\\frac{60}{360} \\times 2\\pi(15) = 5\\pi\\)<br>and \\(\\frac{45}{360} \\times 2\\pi(20) = 5\\pi\\)<br>Ratio \\(= 5\\pi : 5\\pi = \\boxed{1 : 1}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 1:1.</b>","hi":"चाप की लंबाई: \\(\\frac{60}{360} \\times 2\\pi(15) = 5\\pi\\)<br>और \\(\\frac{45}{360} \\times 2\\pi(20) = 5\\pi\\)<br>अनुपात \\(= 5\\pi : 5\\pi = \\boxed{1 : 1}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 1:1 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000070054","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two circles with radii 5 cm and 3 cm have their centers separated by a distance of \\(d\\) cm. If the length of their direct common tangent is exactly twice the length of their transverse common tangent, find the value of \\(d^2\\). [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"5 cm और 3 cm त्रिज्या वाले दो वृत्तों के केंद्रों के बीच की दूरी \\(d\\) cm है। यदि उनकी सीधी उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा की लंबाई तिर्यक उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा की लंबाई की ठीक दोगुनी है, तो \\(d^2\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"84 cm"},"2":{"en":"79 cm"},"3":{"en":"51 cm"},"4":{"en":"105 cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Direct common tangent \\(= \\sqrt{d^2 - (5 - 3)^2} = \\sqrt{d^2 - 4}\\)<br>Transverse common tangent \\(= \\sqrt{d^2 - (5 + 3)^2} = \\sqrt{d^2 - 64}\\)<br>\\(\\sqrt{d^2 - 4} = 2\\sqrt{d^2 - 64}\\)<br>\\(d^2 - 4 = 4d^2 - 256 \\Rightarrow 3d^2 = 252 \\Rightarrow \\boxed{d^2 = 84}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 84 cm.</b>","hi":"सीधी उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा \\(= \\sqrt{d^2 - (5 - 3)^2} = \\sqrt{d^2 - 4}\\)<br>तिर्यक उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखा \\(= \\sqrt{d^2 - (5 + 3)^2} = \\sqrt{d^2 - 64}\\)<br>\\(\\sqrt{d^2 - 4} = 2\\sqrt{d^2 - 64}\\)<br>\\(d^2 - 4 = 4d^2 - 256 \\Rightarrow 3d^2 = 252 \\Rightarrow \\boxed{d^2 = 84}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 84 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000070055","section":"MATH","topic":"Mixture and Alligation","question":{"en":"A vessel contains 90 litres of a mixture of milk and water in the ratio 8:7. How many litres of the mixture should be removed and replaced with pure water so that the ratio of milk to water in the resulting mixture becomes 4:5? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक बर्तन में 90 लीटर दूध और पानी का मिश्रण 8:7 के अनुपात में है। मिश्रण के कितने लीटर निकालकर उसके स्थान पर शुद्ध पानी मिलाया जाए कि परिणामी मिश्रण में दूध और पानी का अनुपात 4:5 हो जाए? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15 litres","hi":"15 लीटर"},"2":{"en":"12 litres","hi":"12 लीटर"},"3":{"en":"6 litres","hi":"6 लीटर"},"4":{"en":"9 litres","hi":"9 लीटर"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Milk \\(= \\frac{8}{15} \\times 90 = 48\\) L, water \\(= 42\\) L<br>Removing \\(x\\) L removes \\(\\frac{8x}{15}\\) L of milk, so milk becomes \\(48 - \\frac{8x}{15}\\)<br>Required: milk \\(= \\frac{4}{9} \\times 90 = 40\\) L<br>\\(48 - \\frac{8x}{15} = 40 \\Rightarrow \\frac{8x}{15} = 8 \\Rightarrow x = \\boxed{15\\ \\text{litres}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 15 litres.</b>","hi":"दूध \\(= \\frac{8}{15} \\times 90 = 48\\) लीटर, पानी \\(= 42\\) लीटर<br>\\(x\\) लीटर निकालने पर \\(\\frac{8x}{15}\\) लीटर दूध निकलता है, अतः दूध \\(48 - \\frac{8x}{15}\\) रह जाता है<br>आवश्यक: दूध \\(= \\frac{4}{9} \\times 90 = 40\\) लीटर<br>\\(48 - \\frac{8x}{15} = 40 \\Rightarrow \\frac{8x}{15} = 8 \\Rightarrow x = \\boxed{15\\ \\text{लीटर}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 15 लीटर है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000070056","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the correctly spelt word.<br><br>The speaker's _________ tone alienated many listeners during the debate. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"supercilious"},"2":{"en":"supercillious"},"3":{"en":"supercileous"},"4":{"en":"suppercillious"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Supercilious (घमंडी, अहंकारी) = behaving as if one is superior to others.</b><br>A supercilious tone naturally alienates listeners, so the word fits the blank.<br><b>supercillious</b> – extra 'l' (-cill-)<br><b>supercileous</b> – 'e' in place of 'i' in the ending (-ious)<br><b>suppercillious</b> – extra 'p' and extra 'l'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): supercilious.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000070057","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with the correctly spelt word.<br><br>The scientist maintained _________ even when her theory was harshly criticized. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"equanamity"},"2":{"en":"equanimity"},"3":{"en":"equinimity"},"4":{"en":"equinammity"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Equanimity (समचित्तता, मानसिक संतुलन) = calmness and composure, especially in a difficult situation.</b><br>She stayed calm under harsh criticism, so 'maintained equanimity' fits.<br><b>equanamity</b> – 'a' in place of 'i' after 'n' (-nim-)<br><b>equinimity</b> – 'i' in place of 'a' after 'u' (equa-)<br><b>equinammity</b> – 'i' for 'a', 'a' for 'i' and a double 'm'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): equanimity.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000070058","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Which of the following is the correct spelling of the word? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Logorrhoea"},"2":{"en":"Logorhoea"},"3":{"en":"Loggorrhoea"},"4":{"en":"Loggorrhea"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Logorrhoea (अत्यधिक बकबक) = a tendency to talk too much.</b><br>Spelling: log-o-<b>rrh</b>-oea, a single 'g' and a double 'r'.<br><b>Logorhoea</b> – single 'r'<br><b>Loggorrhoea</b> – extra 'g'<br><b>Loggorrhea</b> – extra 'g'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Logorrhoea.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000070059","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"The Indian government has appointed a new diplomat to head the official residence and office representing India in France.<br><br>What is the correct one-word substitute for “the official residence and office representing India in France”? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Consulate"},"2":{"en":"Embassy"},"3":{"en":"High Commission"},"4":{"en":"Chancery"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Embassy (दूतावास) = the official residence and office of an ambassador representing his country in a foreign capital.</b><br>France is not a Commonwealth country, so India's mission in Paris is an embassy.<br><b>Consulate (वाणिज्य दूतावास)</b> = office of a consul in a city other than the capital, handling visas and trade<br><b>High Commission (उच्चायोग)</b> = mission of one Commonwealth country in another<br><b>Chancery (कुलाधिकार कार्यालय)</b> = only the office section of an embassy, not the residence<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Embassy.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000070060","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"Choose the correct active form of the given sentence.<br><br>Tomorrow, two hours of free time will be obtained by me. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Tomorrow, I will obtain two hours of free time."},"2":{"en":"Yesterday I obtained two hours of free time."},"3":{"en":"I am obtaining two hours of free time today."},"4":{"en":"I had obtained two hours of free time yesterday."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Simple future passive (will be + V3) → active: Subject + will + V1 + Object.</b><br>'by me' becomes the subject 'I'; 'two hours of free time' becomes the object; 'Tomorrow' stays.<br>Active: Tomorrow, I <b>will obtain</b> two hours of free time.<br>Option 2 – changes the tense to simple past and the time to 'Yesterday'<br>Option 3 – present continuous and 'today', both wrong<br>Option 4 – past perfect and 'yesterday', both wrong<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Tomorrow, I will obtain two hours of free time.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000070061","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Direct Indirect (Narration)","question":{"en":"Complete the sentence in indirect speech.<br><br>\"Have you submitted the assignment yet?\" the teacher asked.<br><br>The teacher asked me _________ the assignment yet. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"if I submit"},"2":{"en":"whether I had submitted"},"3":{"en":"if I have submitted"},"4":{"en":"whether had I submitted"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: A yes/no question is reported with 'if/whether'; past reporting verb changes present perfect to past perfect; the question becomes a statement.</b><br>'you' (the listener) → 'I'; 'have submitted' → 'had submitted'.<br>Indirect: The teacher asked me <b>whether I had submitted</b> the assignment yet.<br>if I submit – wrong tense (simple present)<br>if I have submitted – tense not changed to past perfect<br>whether had I submitted – keeps question word order (verb before subject)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): whether I had submitted.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000070062","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br><br>As the 2024 Paris Olympics approached,<br>P. raising concerns over diplomatic boycotts and the potential exclusion of certain nations,<br>Q. global geopolitical tensions, including conflicts in Eastern Europe and trade disputes among superpowers,<br>R. while the International Olympic Committee attempted to maintain neutrality and ensure an inclusive competition<br>S. cast a shadow over the event’s spirit of international unity and sportsmanship, [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PSQR"},"2":{"en":"SRQP"},"3":{"en":"RSPQ"},"4":{"en":"QSPR"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QSPR</b><br>After the opening clause the sentence needs its subject: <b>Q</b> 'global geopolitical tensions…'.<br><b>S</b> gives the verb for this subject: '…cast a shadow over the event's spirit…'.<br><b>P</b> adds the result with a participle: 'raising concerns over diplomatic boycotts…'.<br><b>R</b> closes with the contrast 'while the International Olympic Committee attempted to maintain neutrality…'.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): QSPR.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000070063","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br><br>In response to persistent inflationary pressures,<br>P. against the risk of prolonged stagnation<br>Q. restrictive monetary policies were implemented,<br>R. by raising interest rates and reducing liquidity<br>S. forcing central banks to balance economic growth [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PRQS"},"2":{"en":"QSRP"},"3":{"en":"SQPR"},"4":{"en":"RPSQ"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QSRP</b><br><b>Q</b> gives the main clause after the opening phrase: 'restrictive monetary policies were implemented,'.<br><b>S</b> follows with its effect: 'forcing central banks to balance economic growth'.<br><b>R</b> tells how this was done: 'by raising interest rates and reducing liquidity'.<br><b>P</b> completes 'balance … against the risk of prolonged stagnation'.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): QSRP.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000070064","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Improve the sentence by selecting the appropriate preposition from the following options.<br><br>She received a gift _____her best friend. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"on"},"2":{"en":"from"},"3":{"en":"of"},"4":{"en":"in"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'receive something from someone' – 'from' shows the source or sender.</b><br>The best friend is the giver, so 'from' is required.<br>Correct sentence: She received a gift <b>from</b> her best friend.<br>on – used for surface or occasion ('a gift on her birthday')<br>of – shows possession or material, not the sender<br>in – shows place or time, not source<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): from.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000070065","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?</b><br><br>1. This led to the development of groundbreaking theories such as Heisenberg’s uncertainty principle and Schrödinger’s wave equation.<br>2. In the early 20<sup>th</sup> century, physicists realized that classical mechanics could not explain certain atomic and subatomic phenomena.<br>3. Quantum mechanics revolutionized technology, enabling advancements in semiconductors, lasers, and quantum computing.<br>4. Scientists like Max Planck and Albert Einstein introduced the idea that energy is quantized, laying the foundation for quantum mechanics.<br>5. Despite its success, the theory remains counterintuitive, challenging our understanding of reality at the fundamental level. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2-4-1-3-5"},"2":{"en":"3-1-4-2-5"},"3":{"en":"1-3-4-2-5"},"4":{"en":"3-2-5-4-1"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 2-4-1-3-5</b><br><b>2</b> opens with the problem: classical mechanics failed in the early 20<sup>th</sup> century.<br><b>4</b> gives the first answer: Planck and Einstein said energy is quantized.<br><b>1</b> 'This led to…' continues from 4 with Heisenberg and Schrödinger.<br><b>3</b> states the practical result: new technology.<br><b>5</b> 'Despite its success' closes the paragraph with a reflection.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 2-4-1-3-5.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000070066","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Which of the following pairs of homonyms can be used to fill in the blanks most suitably?<br><br>He had to _____ his brains trying to remember how he came to be on the shore strewn with _____ and driftwood. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"wrack, rack"},"2":{"en":"rack, rack"},"3":{"en":"rack, wrack"},"4":{"en":"wrack, wrack"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rack one's brains (दिमाग पर ज़ोर डालना) = to think very hard.</b><br><b>Rack</b> fits the first blank: 'rack his brains'.<br><b>Wrack (समुद्री खरपतवार)</b> = seaweed and debris thrown on the shore – fits 'strewn with wrack and driftwood'.<br>Options 1 and 4 use 'wrack' for the idiom; option 2 uses 'rack' (a frame or shelf) for the shore debris.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): rack, wrack.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000070067","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct idiom for the word highlighted in bold.<br><br>\"Mrs. Robinson has three children to support, and she doesn’t make very much money at her job. She is barely <b>keeping her head above water.</b>\" [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Struggling to survive financially"},"2":{"en":"Learning how to swim"},"3":{"en":"Feeling relaxed and stress-free"},"4":{"en":"Living in a house near the water"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Keep one's head above water (किसी तरह गुज़ारा करना) = to just manage to survive, especially with money problems.</b><br>She supports three children on low pay, so she is barely managing financially.<br>Example: With rising rents, many small shops are keeping their heads above water.<br>Learning how to swim (तैरना सीखना) – literal meaning, not the idiom<br>Feeling relaxed and stress-free (तनावमुक्त) – opposite of the situation<br>Living near the water (पानी के पास रहना) – literal, unrelated<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Struggling to survive financially.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000070068","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>In contemporary professional environments, workplace stress has emerged as a pervasive and insidious phenomenon, often undermining both organizational efficiency and employee well-being. Far from being a mere by product of demanding schedules, chronic occupational stress is frequently rooted in deeper systemic issues such as unrealistic expectations, inadequate support structures, and a pervasive culture of constant connectivity. The relentless pursuit of productivity, amplified by technological advancements that blur the boundaries between personal and professional spheres, has exacerbated employees' sense of perpetual obligation.<br><br>Left unchecked, prolonged exposure to high-stress environments can precipitate a range of deleterious outcomes, including burnout, diminished cognitive functioning, and even serious physical health conditions like hypertension and cardiovascular disease. Organizations that fail to recognize and address the underlying causes of stress not only risk elevated turnover rates but also compromise innovation, morale, and overall competitiveness.<br><br>Counteracting workplace stress demands a multi-faceted approach that transcends superficial interventions such as temporary wellness programs or occasional mindfulness workshops. Instead, it requires a fundamental re-evaluation of work design, leadership styles, and organizational priorities. Encouraging open dialogue about mental health, instituting flexible work arrangements, and fostering a culture that genuinely values work-life balance are pivotal steps toward cultivating a more sustainable and humane professional landscape.<br><br><br><b>Which of the following is the correct tense used in the sentence:</b><br><br>\"Left unchecked, prolonged exposure to high-stress environments can precipitate a range of deleterious outcomes...\"? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Past Perfect"},"2":{"en":"Present Simple"},"3":{"en":"Future Perfect"},"4":{"en":"Present Conditional"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…prolonged exposure to high-stress environments can precipitate a range of deleterious outcomes…\"</i><br>The verb is 'can precipitate': present modal 'can' + base verb, stating a general truth. It is in the present simple form.<br>Past Perfect needs 'had + V3' – absent.<br>Future Perfect needs 'will have + V3' – absent.<br>Present Conditional needs 'would + V1' – the sentence uses 'can', not 'would'.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Present Simple.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000070069","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>In contemporary professional environments, workplace stress has emerged as a pervasive and insidious phenomenon, often undermining both organizational efficiency and employee well-being. Far from being a mere by product of demanding schedules, chronic occupational stress is frequently rooted in deeper systemic issues such as unrealistic expectations, inadequate support structures, and a pervasive culture of constant connectivity. The relentless pursuit of productivity, amplified by technological advancements that blur the boundaries between personal and professional spheres, has exacerbated employees' sense of perpetual obligation.<br><br>Left unchecked, prolonged exposure to high-stress environments can precipitate a range of deleterious outcomes, including burnout, diminished cognitive functioning, and even serious physical health conditions like hypertension and cardiovascular disease. Organizations that fail to recognize and address the underlying causes of stress not only risk elevated turnover rates but also compromise innovation, morale, and overall competitiveness.<br><br>Counteracting workplace stress demands a multi-faceted approach that transcends superficial interventions such as temporary wellness programs or occasional mindfulness workshops. Instead, it requires a fundamental re-evaluation of work design, leadership styles, and organizational priorities. Encouraging open dialogue about mental health, instituting flexible work arrangements, and fostering a culture that genuinely values work-life balance are pivotal steps toward cultivating a more sustainable and humane professional landscape.<br><br><br>Identify the grammatical function of the phrase <b>\"Far from being a mere by product of demanding schedules\"</b> in the first paragraph. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It is the main subject of the sentence."},"2":{"en":"It is an introductory phrase modifying the main clause."},"3":{"en":"It is a dependent clause providing a condition."},"4":{"en":"It is a direct object of the verb."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"Far from being a mere by product of demanding schedules, chronic occupational stress is frequently rooted in deeper systemic issues…\"</i><br>The phrase comes before the comma and describes the subject of the main clause, 'chronic occupational stress'. It is an introductory phrase modifying the main clause.<br>Option 1 – the subject is 'chronic occupational stress', not the phrase<br>Option 3 – it has no finite verb, so it is a phrase, not a clause, and it gives no condition<br>Option 4 – the verb 'is rooted' takes no object<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): It is an introductory phrase modifying the main clause.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000070070","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>In contemporary professional environments, workplace stress has emerged as a pervasive and insidious phenomenon, often undermining both organizational efficiency and employee well-being. Far from being a mere by product of demanding schedules, chronic occupational stress is frequently rooted in deeper systemic issues such as unrealistic expectations, inadequate support structures, and a pervasive culture of constant connectivity. The relentless pursuit of productivity, amplified by technological advancements that blur the boundaries between personal and professional spheres, has exacerbated employees' sense of perpetual obligation.<br><br>Left unchecked, prolonged exposure to high-stress environments can precipitate a range of deleterious outcomes, including burnout, diminished cognitive functioning, and even serious physical health conditions like hypertension and cardiovascular disease. Organizations that fail to recognize and address the underlying causes of stress not only risk elevated turnover rates but also compromise innovation, morale, and overall competitiveness.<br><br>Counteracting workplace stress demands a multi-faceted approach that transcends superficial interventions such as temporary wellness programs or occasional mindfulness workshops. Instead, it requires a fundamental re-evaluation of work design, leadership styles, and organizational priorities. Encouraging open dialogue about mental health, instituting flexible work arrangements, and fostering a culture that genuinely values work-life balance are pivotal steps toward cultivating a more sustainable and humane professional landscape.<br><br><br>What is the meaning of the word <b>\"insidious\"</b> as used in the passage? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Open and obvious"},"2":{"en":"Harmless and fleeting"},"3":{"en":"Gradually harmful and subtle"},"4":{"en":"Quickly destructive and visible"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…workplace stress has emerged as a pervasive and insidious phenomenon, often undermining both organizational efficiency and employee well-being.\"</i><br><b>Insidious (कपटी, धीरे-धीरे हानि पहुँचाने वाला)</b> = harmful in a slow, hidden way. Stress quietly 'undermines' efficiency and well-being.<br>Open and obvious (स्पष्ट) – opposite of hidden<br>Harmless and fleeting (हानिरहित, क्षणिक) – the passage calls stress harmful and chronic<br>Quickly destructive and visible (तेज़ी से विनाशकारी) – insidious harm is slow and unseen<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Gradually harmful and subtle.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000070071","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>In contemporary professional environments, workplace stress has emerged as a pervasive and insidious phenomenon, often undermining both organizational efficiency and employee well-being. Far from being a mere by product of demanding schedules, chronic occupational stress is frequently rooted in deeper systemic issues such as unrealistic expectations, inadequate support structures, and a pervasive culture of constant connectivity. The relentless pursuit of productivity, amplified by technological advancements that blur the boundaries between personal and professional spheres, has exacerbated employees' sense of perpetual obligation.<br><br>Left unchecked, prolonged exposure to high-stress environments can precipitate a range of deleterious outcomes, including burnout, diminished cognitive functioning, and even serious physical health conditions like hypertension and cardiovascular disease. Organizations that fail to recognize and address the underlying causes of stress not only risk elevated turnover rates but also compromise innovation, morale, and overall competitiveness.<br><br>Counteracting workplace stress demands a multi-faceted approach that transcends superficial interventions such as temporary wellness programs or occasional mindfulness workshops. Instead, it requires a fundamental re-evaluation of work design, leadership styles, and organizational priorities. Encouraging open dialogue about mental health, instituting flexible work arrangements, and fostering a culture that genuinely values work-life balance are pivotal steps toward cultivating a more sustainable and humane professional landscape.<br><br><br>The word <b>\"deleterious\"</b> most nearly means. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Advantageous"},"2":{"en":"Harmful"},"3":{"en":"Temporary"},"4":{"en":"Curious"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…can precipitate a range of deleterious outcomes, including burnout, diminished cognitive functioning, and even serious physical health conditions…\"</i><br><b>Deleterious (हानिकारक)</b> = causing harm or damage. The examples (burnout, hypertension) are all harmful.<br><b>Advantageous (लाभदायक)</b> = beneficial – opposite<br><b>Temporary (अस्थायी)</b> = lasting a short time – not the sense<br><b>Curious (जिज्ञासु)</b> = eager to know – unrelated<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Harmful.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000070072","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>In contemporary professional environments, workplace stress has emerged as a pervasive and insidious phenomenon, often undermining both organizational efficiency and employee well-being. Far from being a mere by product of demanding schedules, chronic occupational stress is frequently rooted in deeper systemic issues such as unrealistic expectations, inadequate support structures, and a pervasive culture of constant connectivity. The relentless pursuit of productivity, amplified by technological advancements that blur the boundaries between personal and professional spheres, has exacerbated employees' sense of perpetual obligation.<br><br>Left unchecked, prolonged exposure to high-stress environments can precipitate a range of deleterious outcomes, including burnout, diminished cognitive functioning, and even serious physical health conditions like hypertension and cardiovascular disease. Organizations that fail to recognize and address the underlying causes of stress not only risk elevated turnover rates but also compromise innovation, morale, and overall competitiveness.<br><br>Counteracting workplace stress demands a multi-faceted approach that transcends superficial interventions such as temporary wellness programs or occasional mindfulness workshops. Instead, it requires a fundamental re-evaluation of work design, leadership styles, and organizational priorities. Encouraging open dialogue about mental health, instituting flexible work arrangements, and fostering a culture that genuinely values work-life balance are pivotal steps toward cultivating a more sustainable and humane professional landscape.<br><br><br>According to the passage, what is a key failure of organizations when addressing workplace stress? [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"They overly emphasize work-life balance."},"2":{"en":"They rely on short-term or surface-level solutions."},"3":{"en":"They provide excessive flexibility, causing laziness."},"4":{"en":"They hire too many inexperienced employees."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"Counteracting workplace stress demands a multi-faceted approach that transcends superficial interventions such as temporary wellness programs or occasional mindfulness workshops.\"</i><br>The passage criticises superficial, temporary measures, i.e. short-term or surface-level solutions.<br>Option 1 – the passage asks for more work-life balance, not less<br>Option 3 – flexible arrangements are recommended, not blamed<br>Option 4 – hiring is not mentioned<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): They rely on short-term or surface-level solutions.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000070073","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: <b>ESOTERIC</b> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Obscure"},"2":{"en":"Popular"},"3":{"en":"Simple"},"4":{"en":"Common"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Esoteric (गूढ़, रहस्यमय) = understood by only a few people with special knowledge.</b><br><b>Obscure (अस्पष्ट, अप्रसिद्ध)</b> = not well known or hard to understand ✔<br><b>Popular (लोकप्रिय)</b> = liked by many – opposite<br><b>Simple (सरल)</b> = easy to understand – opposite<br><b>Common (सामान्य)</b> = ordinary, widespread – opposite<br>More synonyms: abstruse, arcane, recondite.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Obscure.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000070074","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. <b>Excoriate</b> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Praise"},"2":{"en":"Berate"},"3":{"en":"Condemn"},"4":{"en":"Rebuke"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Excoriate (कड़ी निंदा करना) = to criticise someone very severely.</b><br><b>Praise (प्रशंसा करना)</b> = to express approval ✔<br><b>Berate (डाँटना)</b> = to scold angrily – synonym<br><b>Condemn (निंदा करना)</b> = to express strong disapproval – synonym<br><b>Rebuke (फटकारना)</b> = to reprimand sharply – synonym<br>More antonyms: commend, laud, extol.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Praise.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000070075","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct meaning of idiom:<br><b>Beard the lion in his den</b> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Hide from danger"},"2":{"en":"Flatter a powerful person"},"3":{"en":"Feed captive animals"},"4":{"en":"Confront someone powerful on their own ground"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Beard the lion in his den (शेर की माँद में जाकर ललकारना) = to face or challenge a powerful person in his own territory.</b><br>Example: The young lawyer bearded the lion in his den by questioning the minister in his own office.<br>Hide from danger (खतरे से छिपना) – opposite of facing it<br>Flatter a powerful person (चापलूसी करना) – no challenge involved<br>Feed captive animals (बंदी जानवरों को खिलाना) – literal, unrelated<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Confront someone powerful on their own ground.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000070076","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word. <b>Crepuscular</b> [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Dusk"},"2":{"en":"Diurnal"},"3":{"en":"Dim"},"4":{"en":"Twilight"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Crepuscular (संध्याकालीन, गोधूलि का) = relating to twilight; (of animals) active at dawn and dusk.</b><br><b>Diurnal (दिनचर)</b> = active in full daytime ✔<br><b>Dusk (साँझ)</b> = the darker stage of twilight – related, not opposite<br><b>Dim (धुँधला)</b> = not bright – similar to twilight<br><b>Twilight (गोधूलि)</b> = the time of soft light after sunset – synonym<br>More antonyms: daytime, broad-daylight.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Diurnal.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000070077","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"<b>Select the correct option:</b><br>Despite the scholar's penchant for convoluted prose, his central thesis emerged with surprising ___ in the concluding chapter. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"lucidity"},"2":{"en":"opacity"},"3":{"en":"perversity"},"4":{"en":"tenacity"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'Despite' sets up a contrast – the blank must be the opposite of 'convoluted (complicated) prose'.</b><br><b>Lucidity (स्पष्टता)</b> = clarity of expression – contrasts with convoluted.<br>Correct sentence: …his central thesis emerged with surprising <b>lucidity</b> in the concluding chapter.<br><b>Opacity (अस्पष्टता)</b> = lack of clarity – no contrast<br><b>Perversity (हठधर्मिता, विकृति)</b> = deliberate unreasonableness – does not suit a thesis<br><b>Tenacity (दृढ़ता)</b> = persistence – unrelated to clarity<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): lucidity.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000070078","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"<b>Change the following from active to passive:</b><br>They ought to clean the park. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"The park ought to clean."},"2":{"en":"The park ought to be cleaned."},"3":{"en":"The park ought be cleaned."},"4":{"en":"The park ought to have been cleaned."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: ought to + V1 (active) → ought to + be + V3 (passive).</b><br>Object 'the park' becomes the subject; 'by them' is dropped.<br>Passive: The park <b>ought to be cleaned</b>.<br>Option 1 – 'be' and V3 missing, sentence stays active in form<br>Option 3 – 'to' dropped after 'ought'<br>Option 4 – 'to have been' changes the time to the past (perfect)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The park ought to be cleaned.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000070079","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"<b>Find the part of the sentence that contains an error:</b><br>It is high time the minister (1)/ clarifies his stance on the matter (2)/ rather than leaving it (3)/ open to public speculation. (4) [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"(1)"},"2":{"en":"(2)"},"3":{"en":"(3)"},"4":{"en":"(4)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'It is high time' + subject is followed by the simple past (subjunctive) form of the verb.</b><br>'clarifies' in part (2) must be 'clarified'.<br>Correct sentence: It is high time the minister <b>clarified</b> his stance on the matter rather than leaving it open to public speculation.<br>Parts (1), (3) and (4) are correct: 'rather than + leaving' and 'open to public speculation' are idiomatic.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): (2).</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000070080","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"<b>Convert the sentence provided below from its passive voice structure to an active voice structure:</b><br>The decision is not expected to be reversed by the board despite ongoing protests. [SSC CGL 30/09/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Ongoing protests will force the board to reverse the decision."},"2":{"en":"The board is not expected to reverse the decision despite ongoing protests."},"3":{"en":"It is not expected that the board protests against the decision."},"4":{"en":"Protesters expect the board not to reverse the decision."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'to be + V3' → 'to + V1'; the agent 'the board' becomes the subject of the infinitive.</b><br>Only the infinitive part is converted; 'is not expected' stays as it has no stated agent.<br>Active: The board is not expected <b>to reverse</b> the decision despite ongoing protests.<br>Option 1 – changes the meaning; protests forcing reversal is not stated<br>Option 3 – the board does not protest; the meaning is changed<br>Option 4 – adds 'protesters' as the ones expecting, which is not in the original<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): The board is not expected to reverse the decision despite ongoing protests.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};